#
# prima-materia — chaos magic: Fries, Visual Magick
#
# The harvest of one work of the corpus of pmt:ChaosMagic, kept apart from
# traditions/chaos-magic.ttl, which declares the tradition and the work
# (pmw:VisualMagick) and carries its reading note and harvest counts.
# Harvested complete under prima-materia#893 with two independent extraction
# passes over each of three units, a reconciliation of the second pass against
# the first, and a reading of the whole unit by its integrator. Identifiers
# carry the unit letter: VmA preface and chapters 1-5, VmB chapters 6-8,
# VmC chapters 9-11. Cited by page from the running heads of the full-text
# layer. Signs of success, outcome reports and conditions of failure carry a
# note beginning "Counted as ...".
#

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAuthorFinalAuthorityReaderInvitedImprove a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Author not final authority; reader invited to improve methods"@en, "Autor ohne Letztautorität"@de ;
    skos:definition "The preface presents the methods as open and unfixed: the author claims no final authority and challenges readers to devise better techniques; rote exercises from a perfect master are not offered."@en ;
    skos:note "Preface by Mike Ingalls; statement on fixity of method."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), Preface (by Mike Ingalls), pp. v–vi; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASeedUnitConsciousnessBodyChargeIntelligence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seed: unit of consciousness with body, charge, intelligence"@en, "Same (Saat) als Bewusstseinseinheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "A seed is defined as a conscious unit possessing body, charge and intelligence that grows from potential into actuality when conditions fit; seeds are made, sent and grounded to bring about change in world, life or identity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 9; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASeedsTakeManyMediaSigilOne a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeds take many media; sigil is one variety"@en, "Formen der Saat"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seeds can be visual (sigils), acoustic (tunes, chaos song, mantra), physical (chance objects found on shamanic journeys) or enacted through movement, gesture, rite or lived event; the book uses sigil language but the principles transfer to other media."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 9; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASigilEgoisticNeedDoesRealizeFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sigil of an egoistic need does not realize"@en, "Egoistischer Wunsch verwirklicht sich nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the desire expresses an egoistic need rather than an aspect of true will, the sigil will not come to realization."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFulfilmentDesireThroughSigils."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 9; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFulfilmentDesireThroughSigils a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fulfilment of desire through sigils"@en, "Wunscherfüllung durch Sigillen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any desire can be sigilized; when the desire belongs to true will the sigil attaches to the subconscious current of universal will and manifestation follows in time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 9; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAShamanicSeedGathering a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Shamanic seed gathering"@en, "Schamanisches Sammeln von Kraftobjekten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Go into the wilderness concentrating on the aim and singing power songs; travel in trance wherever the spirits lead; collect every object that draws attention in a special way, meaningful or not; then bless, join and bury the collection in a special place."@en ;
    skos:note "Presented as the probably oldest method of sigil construction; archaeological hoards from Seeland cited as examples."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAToolsSpecificSorcery a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tools for a specific sorcery"@en, "Werkzeuge für einen bestimmten Zauber"@de ;
    skos:definition "A gathered, blessed and buried collection of found objects serves as the instrument of a particular act of sorcery."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAShamanicGatheringYieldsSorceryToolsYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Shamanic gathering yields sorcery tools"@en, "Sammeln ergibt Zauberwerkzeug"@de ;
    skos:definition "The shamanic trance-gathering procedure produces the instrumental collection for a specific sorcery."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmAShamanicSeedGathering ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmAToolsSpecificSorcery ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAGrimoireSigilMagicSquare a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Grimoire sigil on a magic square"@en, "Sigille im magischen Quadrat"@de ;
    skos:definition "Write the name of the spirit or intelligence in Hebrew letters, convert each letter to its number, and trace the number sequence as one continuous line on the matching planetary square; numbers too large for the square are reduced (e.g. 30 becomes 3)."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Israel Regardie's manual on making and using talismans and his Golden Dawn system of magick; it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    skos:note "Example: Zazel on the 3x3 square of Saturn."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 11; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAZazelNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Zazel"@en, "Zazel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Named as the spirit of Saturn, whose sigil is traced on the Saturn square."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Zazel" ;
    pm:nameRole "planetary spirit (Saturn)" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 12; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmABindRunesBinderunen a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Bind-runes (Binderunen)"@en, "Binderunen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Write the desire in runic letters and merge them into one single glyph, much as in Spare’s method."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 12; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAAettPositionRuneCode a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Aett-position rune code"@en, "Aettir-Kode"@de ;
    skos:definition "Encode each rune by its position: number of its aett (family of eight) and its place within it, written e.g. as stroke counts or as branches of a fir-tree figure; related codes use fish or face shapes, and whole words can be shaped as a wheel."@en ;
    skos:note "Refers to the author’s Helrunar for more."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 12; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmASparesLetterReductionSigil a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Spare’s letter-reduction sigil"@en, "Spares Buchstabenmethode"@de ;
    skos:definition "State the desire clearly and briefly, ideally as one word; strike out repeated letters (endurance becomes ENDURAC); combine the remaining letters into a pleasing glyph, simplifying or elaborating at will."@en ;
    skos:note "Called the start of the new era of sigil magick; suitable for all purposes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAPersonalMagicalAlphabetSigils a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal magical alphabet for sigils"@en, "Eigenes magisches Alphabet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ask the deep mind for a script that suits you, then build the glyph from the desire written in that script."@en ;
    skos:note "The way of obtaining such a script from the deep mind is given in chapter 4; see the node on developing a personal magical alphabet (pmp:ChaosMagicVmADevelopingPersonalMagicalAlphabet)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmACustorsIterativeAutomaticDrawingSigil a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Custor’s iterative automatic-drawing sigil"@en, "Custors Methode des automatischen Zeichnens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagine the desire until glowing with it; keeping the desire in focus, cover a sheet with wild spontaneous drawing; close the eyes, concentrate on the desire, relax; once fully relaxed look at the sheet, circle the first part that catches the eye and blot out the rest; copy that portion to the top of a fresh sheet and repeat the whole cycle, for dozens of sheets if needed, until a glyph feels intuitively right; the result may be simplified."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Frater Custor's magazine Phoenix Rising (volume 1, number 2); it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmALookDrawingOnlyAfterFullRelaxationPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Look at the drawing only after full relaxation"@en, "Erst entspannt hinsehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Custor’s method the drawing may be looked at only once the practitioner is fully relaxed."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFullRelaxationBeforeViewingDrawing ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmACustorsIterativeAutomaticDrawingSigil ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFullRelaxationBeforeViewingDrawing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Full relaxation before viewing the drawing"@en, "Volle Entspannung vor dem Betrachten"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Custor's method the practitioner, after covering the sheet and concentrating on the desire with closed eyes, relaxes completely; this state is the condition for looking at what was drawn."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASigilFeelsIntuitivelyRightSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sigil feels intuitively right"@en, "Sigille fühlt sich stimmig an"@de ;
    skos:definition "The iteration is finished when a glyph emerges that intuitively feels correct."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: announced in advance for pmp:ChaosMagicVmACustorsIterativeAutomaticDrawingSigil."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAGlyphDevelopmentCountsPartOperation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Glyph development counts as part of the operation"@en, "Herstellung ist Teil der Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Developing the glyph is itself part of the operation, so laziness is discouraged; the advantage of the drawn method is that the deep mind supplies a glyph in a language it readily understands."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAPracticeSigilDrawingYieldsAestheticFamiliarityYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Practice of sigil drawing yields aesthetic familiarity"@en, "Übung ergibt Ästhetikgespür"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeated drawn-sigil work produces familiarity with sigil aesthetics."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmACustorsIterativeAutomaticDrawingSigil ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFamiliarityFundamentalSigilAesthetics ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFamiliarityFundamentalSigilAesthetics a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Familiarity with fundamental sigil aesthetics"@en, "Gespür für Sigillenästhetik"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through repeated practice one comes to know basic aesthetic laws of sigils."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASixChiaSpiritsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Six Chia spirits"@en, "Sechs Chia-Geister"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spirits of left-hand Taoism evoked by sigils; they match the chakras as their negative, qliphotic mirror images."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Michael Saso, The Teachings of Taoist Master Chuang; it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Chia Spirits" ;
    pm:nameRole "Taoist spirits, qliphotic reflections of the chakras" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAEvocationChiaSpirit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evocation of a Chia spirit"@en, "Evokation eines Chia-Geistes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Calling forth a specific Taoist Chia spirit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAHuangChenNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Huang Chen"@en, "Huang Chen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A Chia-Tzu spirit, one of the six Chia spirits, evoked by a brush-drawn sigil."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Michael Saso, The Teachings of Taoist Master Chuang; it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Huang Chen" ;
    pm:nameRole "Chia-Tzu spirit" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmATaoistEvocationSigilBrushSword a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Taoist evocation sigil by brush and sword"@en, "Taoistische Evokationssigille"@de ;
    skos:definition "The evoking sigil is painted with a brush on paper and also traced with a sword in the air."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Michael Saso, The Teachings of Taoist Master Chuang; it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    skos:note "Author notes resemblance to sigils from the drawing method; brush linework said to be hard."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmABrushSwordSigilYieldsEvocationHuangYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Brush-and-sword sigil yields evocation of Huang Chen"@en, "Sigille ergibt Evokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Taoist sigil drawn by brush and sword is employed for evoking that Chia-Tzu spirit."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmATaoistEvocationSigilBrushSword ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmAEvocationChiaSpirit ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAContinuousLineOverlaidLetters a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous-line overlaid letters"@en, "Fortlaufende Linie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Write the desire as one unbroken line, forming letters as they come, stacked or pointing any direction, then fill the middle of the figure so an illegible amorphous shape results."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAReceivingSigilEntity a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Receiving a sigil from an entity"@en, "Empfangene Sigille"@de ;
    skos:definition "On meeting a spirit, deity or astral being, ask it for a sigil that describes and evokes it; bring the received sign back into manifest reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Received sigils are often incomprehensible to waking mind; examples in Kenneth Grant and the author’s drawings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAReceivedSigilYieldsInterPlaneConnectionYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Received sigil yields inter-plane connection"@en, "Empfangene Sigille ergibt Verbindung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bringing back a received sigil gives the entity easier access and links the planes."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmAReceivingSigilEntity ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmAConnectionBetweenPlanesEntity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAConnectionBetweenPlanesEntity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Connection between planes for an entity"@en, "Verbindung zwischen den Ebenen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A received sigil becomes the manifest side of an intelligence that is itself unmanifest, easing the entity’s access to this plane and the circulation of energy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAReceivedSigilsFitReceiversPersonality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Received sigils fit the receiver’s personality"@en, "Ästhetik empfangener Sigillen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Although the intelligence behind received sigils seems independent, their style usually matches the receiver; the best mix known and unknown elements, half revealed and half hidden."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASigilMustRecallDesire a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sigil must not recall the desire"@en, "Sigille darf nicht an Wunsch erinnern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Common rule of all methods: the finished glyph should not call the original desire to mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAIdentityConflictingCrowdSelves a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Identity as a conflicting crowd of selves"@en, "Identität als Vielheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Conscious identity is a cluster of habits and beliefs, many in conflict; any desire is backed by some sub-personalities and opposed or conditioned by others (ethical, modest, greedy, cynical, sceptical selves, etc.), so clear unified action is rare unless survival, instinct or true will takes over; hence sigils."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmANeutralAbstractShapeBypassesInnerVeto a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Neutral, abstract shape bypasses inner veto"@en, "Neutrale Form umgeht Ego"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because the sigil is abstract, one can work it without engaging the inner pros, cons and vetoes; it is released into the domain of true will and instinct, which decide how and when manifestation occurs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASigilMagickFeedbackLoop a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sigil magick as feedback loop"@en, "Sigillenmagie als Rückkopplung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The desire rises from the deep, gets recognized, is turned into a sigil, cast back into the deep and fulfilled from there; the sorcerer need not settle whether the desire is wilful."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmADoThinkDesireDuringTransmissionCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not think of the desire during transmission"@en, "Nicht an den Wunsch denken"@de ;
    skos:definition "The original desire should be kept out of mind while the sigil is transmitted."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmAEffortlessTransmission ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmASeveralSigilsPickOneLater a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Several sigils, pick one later"@en, "Mehrere Sigillen anlegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sigilize several desires; at a suitable time pick one and work it; ideally its meaning has been forgotten, otherwise pretend not to know what it is for even if memory surfaces."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Austin Osman Spare; it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAPretendedForgettingYieldsFriendlyIndifferenceYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Pretended forgetting yields friendly indifference"@en, "Vorgetäuschtes Vergessen ergibt Gleichgültigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pretending not to know the sigil’s purpose produces the needed indifference."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmASeveralSigilsPickOneLater ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFriendlyIndifference ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFriendlyIndifference a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Friendly indifference"@en, "Freundliche Gleichgültigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "An attitude in which the ego finds no reason to protest or struggle, giving the sigil free passage; Spare named it union through absent-mindedness and summed it up in his formula that it neither matters nor needs to be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAEmotionalChargePoisonsTransmissionFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Emotional charge poisons transmission"@en, "Gefühle vergiften Übertragung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Anxiety, need, fear, hope, lust and similar states block transmission because they bind the sigil to emotions that stop its passage into the deep."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns sigil work in general."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAgainstSparesLongWishSentencesDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against Spare’s long wish-sentences"@en, "Gegen Spares lange Wunschsätze"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spare’s sample formulations in the Book of Pleasure are judged needlessly complicated; the author strips phrases such as my wish and to obtain, reducing the statement to a compound like tiger-strength for a leaner sigil."@en ;
    skos:note "Explicit disagreement with Austin Osman Spare; only Fries's side is read here, so it is entered as a concept and not as pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASigilRequestIntelligenceTrust a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sigil as request to an intelligence; trust"@en, "Sigille als Bitte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like an acupuncture needle, a sigil need not be told its task; touching the relevant aspect lets true will decide whether to add or subtract; sigil magick rests on trust and results may look unpredictable without being wrong."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmATaoistSigilBodyRedInkYellow a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Taoist sigil body: red ink, yellow paper, seal"@en, "Taoistischer Sigillenkörper"@de ;
    skos:definition "Write the sigil with red ink upon yellow paper, optionally stamp it with the sacred seal, burn half the sheet and keep the other half."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Chinese Taoist practice; it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    skos:note "Illustrates that right aesthetics ease transmission."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAOwnExperienceColoursBeforeUsingThemPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Own experience of colours before using them"@en, "Eigene Farberfahrung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Coloured paper and ink are recommended only when the practitioner has lived experience of what colours mean to them."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmALivedKnowledgeWhatColoursMeanOneself ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmATaoistSigilBodyRedInkYellow ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Colour meanings taken from books are useless" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmALivedKnowledgeWhatColoursMeanOneself a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lived knowledge of what colours mean to oneself"@en, "Gelebtes Wissen um die eigene Bedeutung der Farben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Direct personal experience of colours and of their meaning to oneself, gained from life rather than from reference books."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAPaperShapeCorrespondencesScheme a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Paper shape correspondences"@en, "Formentsprechungen des Papiers"@de ;
    skos:definition "Author’s scheme: circle stresses the roundness of the seed, square the solidity of matter, triangle force; choice follows the nature of the desire."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Jan Fries, in Visual Magick" ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAMaterialCorrespondencesSigilBodyScheme a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Material correspondences for the sigil body"@en, "Materialentsprechungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Clay pentacle for material results; enduring stone, metal, bone for lasting effects; bone for matters at the core of one’s being; wood for growing things; metals by planetary attribution."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Jan Fries, in Visual Magick" ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmABoneOnlyIfAssociationsPositiveCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Bone only if its associations are positive"@en, "Knochen nur bei passender Assoziation"@de ;
    skos:definition "If bone evokes death and doom rather than age or essence, inner work is needed before using the material."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmAMaterialCorrespondencesSigilBodyScheme ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmARunicCarvingRubbedAshBlood a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Runic carving rubbed with ash or blood"@en, "Runenritzung mit Asche oder Blut"@de ;
    skos:definition "Carve the signs lightly into wood and rub ash or blood into them for visibility; one’s own blood conveys sincerity and determination."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from rune magicians; it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAImaginedSigilsFullMoon a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Imagined sigils in the full moon"@en, "Sigillen in der Vollmondscheibe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visualize complex sigils as clear red lines projected into the disc of the full moon."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from texts of the Fraternitas Saturni; it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAPlacingAstralSigilVessel a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Placing an astral sigil in a vessel"@en, "Sigille in einem Gefäß"@de ;
    skos:definition "When holding a clear astral image of the sigil is too taxing, place it in a seed shape, treasure chest, chalice or other container and work with that."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmATemporarySigilBodies a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Temporary sigil bodies"@en, "Vergängliche Sigillenkörper"@de ;
    skos:definition "Give the sigil a perishable body: for dream magick draw it, fold a paper boat and float it on water; paint it on the skin in earth colours and dance until sweated off; lay it in berries for birds; scratch it in earth for the rain; burn it; or eat it, washing off ink into water or baking it into bread or cake."@en ;
    skos:note "Water is said to dissolve the carrier and take in the idea; Nema quoted on eating as earthing; invitation to invent more."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmADreamMagickResults a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dream magick results"@en, "Traummagie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Effects in the field of dream magick, sought by a sigil sent off on water."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAPaperBoatSigilYieldsDreamMagickYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Paper-boat sigil yields dream magick"@en, "Papierboot ergibt Traummagie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The paper-boat body on water is the suggested vehicle for dream-magick desires."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmATemporarySigilBodies ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmADreamMagickResults ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAUseNonToxicInkWhenDrinkingCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Use non-toxic ink when drinking sigils"@en, "Ungiftige Tinte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ink washed off to drink must be of a non-toxic kind."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmATemporarySigilBodies ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmADevelopYourOwnMethods a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Develop your own methods"@en, "Eigene Wege entwickeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "The listed techniques are not exhaustive; practitioners are urged to invent their own."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on openness of method."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 1 The Seed, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASigilMessageLivingEntityGateway a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sigil as message, living entity and gateway"@en, "Sigille als Botschaft, Wesen, Tor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Three models: a message capsule signalling the deeper strata of mind, a living being like a seed, and a gateway or channel to a related power zone; it is all these at once, and more."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFamiliarityShapeBeforeTransmissionPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Familiarity with the shape before transmission"@en, "Vertrautheit mit der Form"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before communicating the sigil one must know it well enough to draw it from memory; hence sigils should be simple."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmAKnowingSigilWellEnoughDrawIt ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmABasicTransmissionFormula ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
