pmp:ChaosMagicVmABasicTransmissionFormula a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Basic transmission formula"@en, "Grundformel der Übertragung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Empty yourself, contact the deep, embrace the sigil, let it sink, close the gap, then forget."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASixStepTransmissionFormulaSeries a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Six-step transmission formula"@en, "Sechsschritt-Formel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Author’s ordered scheme of transmission: emptying, contact, embrace, submersion, closing, forgetting."@en ;
    skos:note "Steps not described beyond their naming in the formula are held as their own nodes so that the series has a member at each place; no consequence of skipping a stage is named."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:ChaosMagicVmAVacuitySuspensionConsciousIdentity ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:ChaosMagicVmAMakingContactDeep ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:ChaosMagicVmAEffortlessTransmission ;
    rdf:_4 pmp:ChaosMagicVmALettingSigilSubmerge ;
    rdf:_5 pmp:ChaosMagicVmAClosingGap ;
    rdf:_6 pmp:ChaosMagicVmAForgettingAfterEachWorking ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Fries gives the basic formula as six steps in this order, and each takes its sense from its place: only an emptied mind can reach the deep, the sigil is embraced and let sink only once contact is made, the gap is closed after it has gone down, and forgetting comes last so that the ego cannot follow it." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAMakingContactDeep a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Making contact with the deep"@en, "Kontakt mit der Tiefe aufnehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Second step of the basic transmission formula: once emptied, the practitioner reaches into the deep; the formula names the step without describing it further."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmALettingSigilSubmerge a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting the sigil submerge"@en, "Die Sigille versinken lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fourth step of the basic transmission formula: after embracing the sigil one lets it sink into the deep, without telling it where to go; in the ritual example this happens in the silent phases."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, pp. 22–24; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAClosingGap a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Closing the gap"@en, "Die Lücke schließen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fifth step of the basic transmission formula: after the sigil has gone down, the opening to the deep is shut again before the sigil is forgotten; the formula names the step without describing it further."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAOpeningTransmissionAgainstChargingReleasedEnergyCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Opening is not transmission: against charging with released energy"@en, "Öffnen ist nicht Übertragen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many confuse the opening phase with transmission and try to load released energy from crisis, exhaustion or sex into the sigil; the author, who once held this view himself, calls it mistaken; Spare: no crucifixion is needed."@en ;
    skos:note "Self-correction of the author’s earlier practice."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmAEffortlessTransmission ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAEscalatingForceEndsCrampFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Escalating force ends in cramp"@en, "Mehr Kraft führt zu Krampf"@de ;
    skos:definition "When a charged sigil fails and the magician escalates crisis, ritual, exhaustion or orgasm on the belief that more force works better, the usual outcome is cramp and frustration."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmp:ChaosMagicVmABasicTransmissionFormula."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 23; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAEffortlessTransmission a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Effortless transmission"@en, "Mühelose Übertragung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Open the mind and let the shape fill awareness without forced concentration; focus your whole being on it, feel it deeply, keep the mind void, let awareness merge into the lines and lend the seed sentience; keep attention gentle, calm, relaxed and free of cramp."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 23; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAEffortOnlyOpeningNoneTransmissionPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Effort only for opening, none in transmission"@en, "Mühe nur beim Öffnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Effort may be needed to open the gates, but transmission itself must be effortless; one must be empty to receive."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmAVacuitySuspensionConsciousIdentity ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmAEffortlessTransmission ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 23; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAVisualPhenomenaMayShowDeeperContactSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Visual phenomena may show deeper contact"@en, "Phänomene als Zeichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moving lines, dimming or glowing paper, blurring or doubled vision may indicate contact with deeper levels, though this is not important in itself."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: announced in advance for pmp:ChaosMagicVmAEffortlessTransmission."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 23; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAStrongSensationsEgoInterferenceDuringTransmissionCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Strong sensations and ego interference during transmission"@en, "Starke Empfindungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sinking sigil may stir strange entities, emotions, distractions, spasms or irritating urges and can dislodge waste material; ego may try to stop the work; do not worry, let it pass, do not struggle; deeper trance with lost time sense or trembling is likewise unimportant."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmAEffortlessTransmission ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 23; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAVividRecallDesireFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Vivid recall of the desire"@en, "Lebhafte Erinnerung an den Wunsch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Remembering the desire during transmission is useless because it ties the shape to the fears and longings one wants to avoid; attend only to the form."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmp:ChaosMagicVmAEffortlessTransmission."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 24; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASeedKnowsWay a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The seed knows its way"@en, "Die Saat kennt ihren Weg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Neither the inner self nor the sigil needs instruction on purpose or route through the deep."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 24; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAlternatingExcitementTranquillity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Alternating excitement and tranquillity"@en, "Erregung und Ruhe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Transmission usually alternates: excitement (swaying, shamanic trembling) clears passages and regulates trance depth, while tranquillity carries the message through; sensations should neither be fought nor sought."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 24; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmACrampBlocksTransmissionFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cramp blocks transmission"@en, "Krampf blockiert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cramp stops the transmission and binds the sigil to troublesome emotions."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmp:ChaosMagicVmAEffortlessTransmission."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 24; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmANewMoonFullMoonWorkingPeriod a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "New moon to full moon working period"@en, "Neumond bis Vollmond"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make the sigil at new moon and work it whenever inclined until full moon; stop each session when you feel you have had enough and resume another time."@en ;
    skos:note "Lunar phases serve as confirmation, the working does not depend on them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 24; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAForgettingAfterEachWorking a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Forgetting after each working"@en, "Vergessen nach jeder Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "After each session forget and ignore the sigil, aided by a mood of friendly indifference."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Austin Osman Spare; it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 24; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASimplicityTransmissionHardCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Simplicity of transmission is hard"@en, "Einfachheit ist schwer"@de ;
    skos:definition "The plain simplicity of transmission can prove a difficult achievement."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmAEffortlessTransmission ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 24; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmARitualExampleExhaustionTransmissionRelease a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual example: exhaustion, transmission, release"@en, "Ritualbeispiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "1 Exhaustion: walk a long way to a place of power (mountain top, grove, lake), avoid everyday thoughts, sweat; hard conditions such as night, cold or storm help unsettle ego; use a mantra. 2 Transmission: ritual opening and purification, invoke gods, spirits or totems, enter trance by dance, chant and music; lay out the sigil and play a simple instrument while gazing, alternating music and silence; trembling is fine without cramp; let the sigil sink in the silent phases without willing. 3 Release: kiss and bury the sigil, place flowers, sprinkle wine, stand or dance nearby, give thanks, close and leave."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAThreeStageRitualFrameSeries a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Three-stage ritual frame"@en, "Dreistufiger Ritualrahmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Author’s ordered frame for transmission rites: exhaustion, transmission, release."@en ;
    skos:note "No consequence of skipping a stage is named."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:ChaosMagicVmAPhysicalExhaustion ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:ChaosMagicVmAEffortlessTransmission ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:ChaosMagicVmAReleaseKissingBuryingSigil ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The ritual example runs in three numbered stages, exhaustion, transmission and release; the exhaustion opens the gates the transmission needs, and the release closes the rite after the sigil has been taken in. Fries offers it as one example frame among others." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmANeitherResistNorIndulgeExcitementCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Neither resist nor indulge excitement"@en, "Erregung weder abwehren noch suchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Go with the flow during the rite; trembling is acceptable only without strain."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmARitualExampleExhaustionTransmissionRelease ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAReleaseKissingBuryingSigil a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Release: kissing and burying the sigil"@en, "Entlassung: die Sigille küssen und begraben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Third stage of the ritual example: when done, kiss the sigil and bury it, lay flowers on the earth over it and sprinkle wine there, stand or dance nearby, give thanks, close the rite and leave."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAIntrovertedRouteDeepSelfHypnosis a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Introverted route: deep self-hypnosis"@en, "Tiefe Selbsthypnose"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of extroverted music, chant and wilderness, reach the transmission trance by deep self-hypnosis."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmALoveRequiredSexualMagickPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Love required in sexual magick"@en, "Liebe in Sexualmagie"@de ;
    skos:definition "In sexual magick union transcends ego through love."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmALoveThatCarriesPartnersBeyondEgo ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmASigilFocusedOrgasm ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without love identity is not transcended and transmission cannot happen" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmALoveThatCarriesPartnersBeyondEgo a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Love that carries the partners beyond ego"@en, "Liebe, die über das Ich hinausträgt"@de ;
    skos:definition "In sexual magick the feeling of love between trusting partners is what lets identity be transcended during union, so that a sigil can be transmitted."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, pp. 25–26; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmADoOverburdenSexualPartnerUnknowingPartnerCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not overburden a sexual partner; no unknowing partner"@en, "Partner nicht überlasten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mutual trust means not loading a partner with sigils or energies they cannot handle; using an uninformed prostitute reduces the magical union to masturbation."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmASigilFocusedOrgasm ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmACrowleysSexMagickDiariesNegativeExampleDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Crowley’s sex-magick diaries as a negative example"@en, "Crowleys Tagebücher als Negativbeispiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Crowley’s Rex de Arte Regia diaries are held up as an example of how not to practise sexual magick."@en ;
    skos:note "Explicit disagreement with Aleister Crowley; only Fries's side is read here, so it is entered as a concept and not as pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAgainstWorkingSigilUntilItManifestsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Against working a sigil until it manifests"@en, "Nicht bis zur Manifestation bearbeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Contrary to some magicians’ advice, the sigil manifests when conditions suit it; if they do not, stubborn persistence cannot force the result and the futile effort unbalances the mind, causing frustration and cramp."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmABasicTransmissionFormula ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmASigilChargedObsessingGuest a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sigil charged by an obsessing guest"@en, "Ladung durch besessenen Gast"@de ;
    skos:definition "Work with a god, beast or spirit in direct possession (as in Asiatic shamanism, Voodoo or Norse seidr); the guest acting through the body may take control and charge the sigil itself, with shouting, trembling and convulsions possible; no emptying of mind is needed because the deep has risen to the surface."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAObsessionSessionsCanBecomeWildCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Obsession sessions can become wild"@en, "Wilde Sitzungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Depending on the guest, such a session may involve much shouting, trembling and convulsions."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmASigilChargedObsessingGuest ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmADirectChargingSigilPossessingEntity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Direct charging of a sigil by a possessing entity"@en, "Ladung durch den Gast"@de ;
    skos:definition "The presence of the guest suspends ego interference so that the entity charges the sigil directly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAObsessionWorkingYieldsGuestChargingYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Obsession working yields guest charging"@en, "Besessenheit ergibt Ladung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Direct obsession lets the guest charge the sigil."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmASigilChargedObsessingGuest ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmADirectChargingSigilPossessingEntity ;
