pmc:ChaosMagicVmALifeConditionsGroundSeed a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Life conditions are the ground of the seed"@en, "Lebensbedingungen als Boden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The conditions one lives in are the soil; in wrong ground the seed suspends activity and waits; efficiency depends on conditions set by true will, not on the magician’s effort."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAchievingWillThroughUnknownAvenues a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Achieving will through unknown avenues"@en, "Umgehung von Hindernissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sigils let one reach aims blocked for conscious will, bypassing adverse conditions and identity’s censorship through routes one does not know."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAThinkingResultsBindsOutcomeFailingChannelsFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Thinking of results binds the outcome to failing channels"@en, "Ergebnisdenken blockiert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thinking of results during transmission ties the mind to the desired routes, which are usually exactly the ones that do not work; the conscious self is often the main obstacle."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmp:ChaosMagicVmAEffortlessTransmission."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASubconsciousActiveAgentChargingNeeded a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The subconscious is the active agent; no charging needed"@en, "Keine Ladung nötig"@de ;
    skos:definition "The active agency is the subconscious self, whose power dwarfs consciously raised force; a well-transmitted sigil enters the currents of true will and instinct and becomes irresistible without being energized."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASigilAgainstTrueWillRemainsLatentFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sigil against true will remains latent and is expelled"@en, "Sigille gegen wahren Willen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A sigil contrary to one’s own or another person’s true will gets no force, stays latent and is expelled as alien material through confrontation, nightmare, crisis or dark astral passages; some sigils never manifest."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFulfilmentDesireThroughSigils."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmADarkGodsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The dark gods"@en, "Die dunklen Götter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Said to help purify the soul by showing one what one foolishly desired, so the waste can be digested and recycled."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "dark gods" ;
    pm:nameRole "purifying powers of the deep" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAManifestationUnexpectedFormSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Manifestation in unexpected form"@en, "Unerwartete Erfüllung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A sigil may count as fulfilled when the need evaporates or the desire is surpassed through illumination or personality change rather than by getting the wished-for thing."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: announced in advance for pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFulfilmentDesireThroughSigils."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAHibernatingSigils a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hibernating sigils"@en, "Ruhende Sigillen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sigils blocked by adverse conditions or wrong timing lie dormant and wait for their season; they may incarnate when habits and beliefs are disrupted by crisis, illness or lifestyle change, since identity forms the climate that selects which seeds grow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAccumulatedSigilsImpossibleDesireCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Accumulated sigils for an impossible desire"@en, "Angestaute Sigillen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many suspended sigils for one impossible desire can seriously unbalance the mind, discharging as wish-phantasms, hallucination or symbolic acting-out, or erupting violently and transforming one from within."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmAHibernatingSigils ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAOverEagerChargingClosesGatesFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Over-eager charging closes the gates"@en, "Übereifer schließt die Tore"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magicians who keep increasing charges, crisis, formulae or secret sex rites become frantic, fight fear of failure and grow so fixed on the refused desire that the gates shut by reflex."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFulfilmentDesireThroughSigils."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAStubbornPersistenceEgoDrivenCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Stubborn persistence is ego-driven"@en, "Starrsinn ist Ego"@de ;
    skos:definition "Running repeatedly against a wall usually stems from ego’s belief that it knows its will; failure threatens ego, so the struggle is relabelled challenge or ordeal rather than admitting error."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFulfilmentDesireThroughSigils ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAGentlePlacementLivingRightConditions a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Gentle placement and living the right conditions"@en, "Sanft säen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Under right conditions a sigil needs little effort and develops with surprising grace; part of the task is to live the conditions, e.g. developing talents; a belief such as being unable to draw must first be changed by the sigil or bypassed when inhibitions are low."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmABeliefsObstructSigilsFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Beliefs obstruct sigils"@en, "Glaubenssätze als Hindernis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fixed beliefs, convictions, necessities, habits, conditioned reflexes and routines are major obstacles to a sigil working."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFulfilmentDesireThroughSigils."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmADeathPosturePeriodicBeliefDissolution a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Death posture: periodic belief dissolution"@en, "Todeshaltung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Regularly dissolve every belief one becomes aware of (Spare’s death posture) and let the personality rebuild itself from emptiness; beliefs that are true return intact afterwards."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Austin Osman Spare; it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAvoidSelectiveBeliefDissolutionCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Avoid selective belief dissolution"@en, "Keine halbe Auflösung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Exempting a favoured belief as truth while dropping the rest is sloppy; all noticed beliefs must go."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmADeathPosturePeriodicBeliefDissolution ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmABeliefDissolutionYieldsFluidityYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Belief dissolution yields fluidity"@en, "Auflösung ergibt Wandlungsfähigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Periodic belief dissolution produces fluidity for wilful change."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmADeathPosturePeriodicBeliefDissolution ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFluidityAcceptWilfulChange ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFluidityAcceptWilfulChange a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fluidity to accept wilful change"@en, "Wandlungsfähigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Regular shredding of beliefs keeps one supple enough to accept willed change easily and gives the self room to adapt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAWuWeiHonestLivingOverRitual a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wu Wei and honest living over ritual"@en, "Wu Wei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spare relied less on ritual than on honest living; non-doing or effortless action is the suitable state."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAnxietyAboutResultsPreventsIncarnationFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Anxiety about results prevents incarnation"@en, "Ergebnisangst verhindert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some desires, especially for psychological change, cannot manifest while one worries about results, since ego tries to censor, hurry or steer the process; plants do not grow faster when pulled."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFulfilmentDesireThroughSigils."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmALearningForgetSigil a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Learning to forget the sigil"@en, "Vergessen lernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pretend ignorance of the sigil’s purpose; whenever the memory comes back, tell yourself it is probably mistaken, surely unimportant and cannot be known for certain; this play-acting creates indifference and soon genuine forgetting."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAPretendingYieldsRealForgettingYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Pretending yields real forgetting"@en, "Vortäuschen ergibt Vergessen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The pretence procedure leads to actual forgetting."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmALearningForgetSigil ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmADeliberateForgetfulness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmADeliberateForgetfulness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deliberate forgetfulness"@en, "Absichtliches Vergessen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to imagine something away and truly forget the sigilized desire."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASuccessRecognizedOnlyRetrospectSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Success is recognized only in retrospect"@en, "Erfolg erst rückblickend"@de ;
    skos:definition "It becomes clear that the technique worked only when the new thing has arrived or when, looking back, one sees through former illusions; this demands confidence."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: announced in advance for sigil work in general."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAZosKiaSophisticatedNaivety a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Zos Kia and sophisticated naivety"@en, "Zos Kia"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spare’s Zos Kia, close to Taoism, cultivates open honesty, a refined naivety, comfortable acceptance of paradox and life beyond being versus voidness; the sigil worker never knows for certain and is always surprised."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmADeepOnesNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Deep Ones"@en, "Die Tiefen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Held to care for whatever is handed into their realm; joy counts for more than refined technique."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Deep Ones" ;
    pm:nameRole "powers of the deep mind" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 2 The Ritual, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAgainstSpiritualistClaimAutomaticSpiritMadeDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the spiritualist claim of automatic, spirit-made art"@en, "Gegen spiritistische Automatik"@de ;
    skos:definition "The label automatic is called misleading; spiritualist mediums who credit spirits of great artists for their drawings avoid responsibility for their own talent and show so much ego that dramatic trance effects are needed; Thelemites need no such measures since creativity lies within everyone."@en ;
    skos:note "Explicit disagreement with the Spiritualist/Theosophist medium tradition; only Fries's side is read here, so it is entered as a concept and not as pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', p. 32; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmANamingDrawingsSourceUnimportant a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Naming of the drawing’s source is unimportant"@en, "Quelle der Zeichnung unwichtig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whether the source is called spirits, gods, demons, inner genius or subconscious does not matter; cooperation with it makes total possession unnecessary, and ideally the act is plain and natural; what counts is that a living picture emerges."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAConsciousSubconsciousSelfArt a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Conscious and subconscious self in art"@en, "Bewusstes und unbewusstes Selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "The conscious self learns seeing and drawing by observing and practising; the subconscious self erupts in uncontrolled creativity and is developed by dreaming, wild living and breaking restrictions; it needs release, not training; good art balances power from the one with shape from the other; children lose spontaneous drawing once they learn convention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASubconsciousDrawingUnconscious a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Subconscious drawing is not unconscious"@en, "Nicht unbewusst"@de ;
    skos:definition "All art is conscious; only the sense of I and control is sometimes forgotten in intense creation, so one watches oneself at work; the two attitudes shade into each other."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAInspiredSpontaneousDrawing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inspired spontaneous drawing"@en, "Inspiriertes spontanes Zeichnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The recovered childlike ability to let the hand move freely and let images come through with little deliberation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', pp. 34–35 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAEffortDeliberateControlFixationResultsCrampFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Effort, deliberate control, fixation on results, cramp"@en, "Mühe, Absicht, Ergebnisfixierung, Krampf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Long-held belief in one’s inability to draw keeps the hand from moving freely; the main obstacles are effort, deliberation, fixation on results and cramp."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmc:ChaosMagicVmAInspiredSpontaneousDrawing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', pp. 34–35 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFearOnesOwnAbilityUrgeQuitCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Fear of one’s own ability; urge to quit"@en, "Angst vor eigener Begabung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some beginners fall into crisis when shown they can draw, others are frightened by strange convulsions from unacknowledged parts of identity; the urge to deny talent and stop can be overwhelming."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmACirclesSpiralsExercise ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', pp. 34–35 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmACirclesSpiralsExercise a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Circles and spirals exercise"@en, "Kreise und Spiralen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use many large, tough, cheap sheets (A3 or bigger, wallpaper, packing paper) and soft pencils for thick lines; cover sheet after sheet with swiftly rotating circles and spirals, watch the hand, change grip, then work with eyes closed and vary speed and pressure; fill dozens of sheets even if boring; then try other shapes needing little thought, at least two pages each."@en ;
    skos:note "Includes the instruction to start in large format and use paper without hesitation, which pass A also recorded as a separate prerequisite; it is folded in here."@en ;
    skos:note "Thin hard-pencil lines are for later inking."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', pp. 34–35 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASwiftPowerfulHandMovement a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Swift, powerful hand movement"@en, "Kraftvolle Handbewegung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Habituating the hand to drive the pen with force, intensity and speed; the pattern matters less than this."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', pp. 34–35 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmACircleExercisesYieldPowerfulHandMovementYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Circle exercises yield powerful hand movement"@en, "Kreisübung ergibt Handkraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeated circle, spiral and abandon-shape exercises accustom the hand to swift powerful movement."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmACirclesSpiralsExercise ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmASwiftPowerfulHandMovement ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', pp. 34–35 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmABeliefThatOnesOutputInadequateFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief that one’s output is inadequate"@en, "Glaube an unzureichende Ergebnisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "The feeling of failure restricts free movement of the hand, visible in the pencil line."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmc:ChaosMagicVmAInspiredSpontaneousDrawing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', p. 36; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASaltSulphurMercuryBeginnersTroublesScheme a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Salt, Sulphur, Mercury: beginners’ troubles"@en, "Salz, Schwefel, Quecksilber"@de ;
    skos:definition "Author’s classification of three kinds of beginner trouble by the alchemical principles, each with its own remedy."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Jan Fries, in Visual Magick" ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
