pmc:ChaosMagicVmASulphurSymptomsFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sulphur symptoms"@en, "Schwefel-Symptome"@de ;
    skos:definition "Uneven bursts of force driven by temper, weakness alternating with explosions, hurry, impatience, broken pencil tips and torn paper."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmp:ChaosMagicVmACirclesSpiralsExercise."@en ;
    skos:note "Remedy: keep temper and release power as a steady flow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', p. 36; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAMercurySymptomsFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mercury symptoms"@en, "Quecksilber-Symptome"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thin wavering lines as if afraid to touch the paper, fear of commitment, weak frail or breaking lines."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmp:ChaosMagicVmACirclesSpiralsExercise."@en ;
    skos:note "Remedy: no eraser at all, keep work large, move the pencil decisively."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', p. 36; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmARepairWorkKillsImpulseCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Repair work kills the impulse"@en, "Nachbessern tötet den Impuls"@de ;
    skos:definition "Falling into doubt and losing the impulse through correcting is dangerous; such cases should not use an eraser."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmACirclesSpiralsExercise ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
