pmc:ChaosMagicVmAHealingGivingFormRepressedHorrors a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing by giving form to repressed horrors"@en, "Heilung durch Gestaltung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spontaneous drawing lets the inner self discharge repressed material; confronting and giving shape to one’s horrors may heal, while denying them harms the whole being."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmADoCensorDarkDrawingsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not censor dark drawings"@en, "Nicht zensieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some drawings will look terrible, sick or disgusting; do not look away, face the demons raised without fear or loathing; seeking only beauty restricts, and restricting one aspect soon stagnates all of one’s art."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmASparesTrainingFreeHand ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAWorkingWithoutSpecificCreativeAgent a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Working without a specific creative agent"@en, "Ohne bestimmte Instanz"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practice is taught without reference to any particular being doing the drawing; orthodox mediums who seek a special spirit or angel cramp themselves with questions about what it would draw and limit scope before beginning."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAEvokeAlternativePersonalitiesDrawingOnlyAfterPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Evoke alternative personalities for drawing only after experience"@en, "Erst Übung, dann Evokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only when well practised may one call one of one’s alternative personalities, such as gods, demons, spirits or power beasts, to do the drawing, and experience in shamanic possession should come first."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmAInspiredSpontaneousDrawing, pmp:ChaosMagicVmASigilChargedObsessingGuest ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmADrawingThroughEvokedAlternativePersonality ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmADrawingThroughEvokedAlternativePersonality a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Drawing through an evoked alternative personality"@en, "Zeichnen durch eine gerufene andere Persönlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once spontaneous drawing is well practised, call one of one's alternative personalities (a god, demon, spirit or power beast) and let it do the drawing; experience of shamanic possession should come first."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 3 'Automatic Drawing', p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASigilsGuaranteedResultsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Sigils are no guaranteed results"@en, "Keine Erfolgsgarantie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sigils, like sex magick and drugs, have been misused by the result-hungry; they are not a limitless account with guaranteed satisfaction."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFulfilmentDesireThroughSigils ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
