pmc:ChaosMagicVmASpareGrantTooCrypticMethodConfusedDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spare and Grant too cryptic; method confused"@en, "Spare und Grant zu kryptisch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spare’s writings and Kenneth Grant’s presentation of them are judged too obscure for a broad audience, and many individuals and organizations have muddled the method’s basic simplicity."@en ;
    skos:note "Explicit disagreement with Austin Osman Spare and Kenneth Grant; only Fries's side is read here, so it is entered as a concept and not as pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 4 Sigils, Sex and Beyond, p. 42; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmATrueWillTechniqueDecidesManifestation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "True will, not technique, decides manifestation"@en, "Wahrer Wille entscheidet"@de ;
    skos:definition "A cure-all should not be sought in sigil technique but in true will, which decides if a sigil can manifest."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 4 Sigils, Sex and Beyond, p. 42; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAuthorsIgnoreThatSigilsCanFail a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Authors ignore that sigils can fail"@en, "Scheitern wird verschwiegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most sigil authors overlook that sigils can fail, treating failure as an insult to the mage’s power to be overcome by stronger techniques, like reaching for an electric drill where a needle fails."@en ;
    skos:note "Disagreement with unnamed authors."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 4 Sigils, Sex and Beyond, p. 42; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAYogSothothNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Yog-Sothoth"@en, "Yog-Sothoth"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cited as an interlocutor who assures the author that chaos magick is merely a nice label for organised non-conformity."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Yog-Sothoth" ;
    pm:nameRole "entity speaking to the author (ironic aside)" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
