pmc:ChaosMagicVmALustResultEgoDiseaseFailureMay a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lust of result as ego disease; failure may be wilful"@en, "Ergebnisgier als Ego-Krankheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The constant urge for more power and better results ignores that lust of result is an illness of ego and that failure can at times be willed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 4 Sigils, Sex and Beyond, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmABeginnersWithoutBeliefGetGoodResultsSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Beginners without belief get good results"@en, "Anfänger haben Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Complete beginners, even without any belief in sigils, obtain good results, while pompous masters insisting on their will keep struggling against their fallibility."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report: reported results, not a sign announced in advance for sigil work in general."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 4 Sigils, Sex and Beyond, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAuthorsOwnFailuresThroughEffortStrainFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Author’s own failures through effort and strain"@en, "Eigene Fehler des Autors"@de ;
    skos:definition "In over a decade of sigil practice the author met failure with more effort and strain until cramp became routine."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the author's own report of failing, entered as an outcome report of failure; it concerns sigil work in general."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
