pmc:ChaosMagicVmACrampProtectiveMechanism a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cramp as protective mechanism"@en, "Krampf als Schutz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mental and physical cramp can guard against an intruding hostile power or foreign element tied to unpleasant feelings; it stops the sigil getting through."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 4 Sigils, Sex and Beyond, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmATextWrittenShowSigilMagickSimple a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Text written to show sigil magick as simple and natural"@en, "Einfachheit der Sigillenmagie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author needed years to unlearn accumulated misconceptions; the book aims to show sigil magick as simple and natural; the drawing exercises are not exotic or exalted but useful for setting pen to paper playfully."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on the status of the methods."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
