pmc:ChaosMagicVmASpeakingHeartOverMemorizedInvocations a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Speaking from the heart over memorized invocations"@en, "Aus dem Herzen sprechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magick becomes easy once one again trusts innocence, simplicity and immediate inspiration; heartfelt speech plus freestyle chaos language and chanting gives livelier results than memorized divine names; the belief that real magick must be hard should be changed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 4 Sigils, Sex and Beyond, pp. 45–46 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAHeavyRitualConsciousStaging a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heavy ritual as conscious staging"@en, "Schweres Ritual als Inszenierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hours of temple layout, robes, banishings and invocations are the conscious mind’s effort to set the scene for an operation mainly run by the subconscious; they need not be dropped but one should be able to work without them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 4 Sigils, Sex and Beyond, pp. 45–46 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAConversingDeepMindAboutSigil a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Conversing with the deep mind about a sigil"@en, "Das tiefe Selbst um Hilfe bitten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Close the eyes and address the deep mind informally: say you have a sigil for something vital whose purpose you forgot and ask for help in transmitting it; stay open to feedback as images, sounds, words or feelings; if unclear, ask it to strengthen the signal for yes and weaken it for no; if positive, announce you will open your eyes, gaze at the sigil and ask it to let the message through and sink to the current of will."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 4 Sigils, Sex and Beyond, p. 47; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAPositiveSignalDeepMindSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Positive signal from the deep mind"@en, "Positives Signal"@de ;
    skos:definition "A positive response, or a signal that grows stronger on request, shows willingness to cooperate and clears the way for gazing at the sigil."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: announced in advance for pmp:ChaosMagicVmAConversingDeepMindAboutSigil."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 4 Sigils, Sex and Beyond, p. 47; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

