pmc:ChaosMagicVmAContactCommunicationDeepMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Contact and communication with the deep mind"@en, "Kontakt mit dem tiefen Selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creative visualization can serve the mage to reach and converse with the deep mind, however it is named (gods, genius, ally, guardian angel, totem, patron demon)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 52; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAImaginationPlasticMediumInnerSenses a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Imagination as plastic medium of inner senses"@en, "Imagination als plastisches Medium"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagination is a key to magick: a malleable medium that gives form to beliefs and so creates, sustains and destroys the realities believed in; it is something the inner senses do."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 52; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmASensoryInventoryRecollection a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensory inventory of recollection"@en, "Sinnesinventur der Erinnerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Think of a tree and notice which sensory data arise (shape, wood, sound of foliage, smell, taste, memories); then do the same for sea, mountain and forest, workplace, childhood home, temple, lover, noting which senses are present, absent or preferred."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 53; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmARealityHabitualSelectionDeepMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality as habitual selection by the deep mind"@en, "Wirklichkeit als Auswahl"@de ;
    skos:definition "The deep mind filters the flood of sensory data by priorities into a representation most call reality; a shared objective reality is a scientific fable; each lives in a self-made selection shaped by history, nature, work and will; the selection runs by habit, so specialists, phobics, Marxists and magicians each perceive their own world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 54; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASelectingRealityWorthLiving a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Selecting a reality worth living in"@en, "Eine lebenswerte Wirklichkeit wählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Remembering that one lives in a selection allows one to choose a reality worth inhabiting."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 55; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAExerciseOneSpeakingSensesAloud a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exercise one: speaking the senses aloud"@en, "Übung eins: Sinne aussprechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Settle comfortably, breathe deeply a few times and say aloud what you are perceiving, sense by sense: first touch (book in hands, body in chair, breath in belly, air on skin), going deeply into it; then hearing; then sight; repeat for a while and in varied surroundings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 55; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

