pmp:ChaosMagicVmAExerciseOneVariationsVoiceModes a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exercise one variations: voice modes"@en, "Variationen: Stimmlagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "While describing the senses: 1 use a friendly voice one would like to be addressed in; 2 speak fast, loud, ever more excited; 3 try the sonorous, droning, self-important ceremonial voice; 4 speak ever slower and softer, two or three words per breath, letting it lead into a restful natural trance; 5 then lower the voice to a whisper and continue with the inner voice, noticing whether it is friendly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 56; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

