pmc:ChaosMagicVmAUsingPhysicalEyesYieldsOnlyDarknessFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Using physical eyes yields only darkness"@en, "Nur Dunkelheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who keep trying to see with the physical eyes behind closed lids find only darkness, because inner vision is imagined rather than seen."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmc:ChaosMagicVmAInnerVision."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 59; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAThinkingRapidMultisensoryInnerOperation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Thinking as rapid multisensory inner operation"@en, "Schnelles inneres Denken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recalling what anything looks like already uses inner vision; sequences of inner seeing, feeling and self-talk run in under a second, so consciousness registers only the result as having thought."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 59; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFavouriteSensesAllSensesLearnable a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Favourite senses; all senses learnable"@en, "Lieblingssinne"@de ;
    skos:definition "People differ in favoured inner senses (inner hearing, vision, feeling); probably all senses work all the time but consciousness specializes, which helps and restricts; typing oneself as one type is wrong, and the weaker senses should be trained as well."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 60; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmATrainingWeakerSenses a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Training the weaker senses"@en, "Schwächere Sinne schulen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever has one well-developed sense should cultivate the others to the same level."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 60; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAMagickNeedsGoodImagination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magick needs good imagination"@en, "Magie braucht Vorstellungskraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "A good imagination is required for magick."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 60; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAMultisensoryGodFormImagining a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Multisensory god-form imagining"@en, "Gottesform mit allen Sinnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagine a deity with sight, sound and feeling working together, each channel supporting the others, rather than only hearing its names, feeling awe or seeing it with scenery."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 60; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAllSensesNeededIntenseContactPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "All senses needed for intense contact"@en, "Alle Sinne nötig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intense contact with a god-form requires the use of all senses together."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmATrainingWeakerSenses ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmAIntenseContactGodForm ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Working from a favourite sense alone is not good enough for intense contact" ;
