pmp:ChaosMagicVmAKeepTalkingRepetitionPauses a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Keep talking: repetition and pauses"@en, "Weitersprechen mit Wiederholung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Say anything, with no right or wrong; keep talking; when nothing new comes, repeat what was said until something new arises; use pauses of intense silence to clear the senses; in slow hypnotic speech repetitions and pauses deepen the trance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 62; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFreeSpeechPracticeYieldsTrustDeepYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Free speech practice yields trust in the deep mind"@en, "Freies Sprechen ergibt Vertrauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Free talking over time yields confidence that the deep mind will find words."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmAKeepTalkingRepetitionPauses ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmATrustDeepMindSupplyWords ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 62; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmATrustDeepMindSupplyWords a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trust in the deep mind to supply words"@en, "Vertrauen in die Worte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Long practice of free speech teaches that the deep mind can be trusted to find the right words."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 62; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmATranceNeedsRelaxedBodyTrancesEveryday a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trance needs no relaxed body; trances are everyday"@en, "Trance ohne Entspannung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Contrary to the meditative model of a resting body, hypnotherapists, shamans, voodoo and chaos practitioners know trance does not require passivity; most trances arise naturally, people enter them dozens of times daily, and willed trance differs only in degree."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 62; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAbsorbedDissociatedEverydayTrances a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Absorbed and dissociated everyday trances"@en, "Zwei Alltagstrancen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rapt fascination with an outside stimulus (an engaging lesson) and boredom-driven turning inward (a dull lesson) are both trances; whether inner absorption is called daydream or hallucination depends on judging it natural or pathological; depression and love also narrow outer awareness; Erickson: trance narrows attention while intensifying it."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Milton H. Erickson (definition of trance); it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 63; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAuthorsPaintingTrance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Author’s painting trance"@en, "Maltrance des Autors"@de ;
    skos:definition "When painting the author is absorbed for hours, forgets food, drink and rest, and on finishing suddenly notices his body and total exhaustion."@en ;
    skos:note "First-person illustration of absorbed trance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 63; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAGoingInwardDescribing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Going inward and describing"@en, "Nach innen gehen und beschreiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Turn attention inward and describe everything perceived there; inner awareness grows stronger and more vivid."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from some schools of psychotherapy; it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 64; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmANepaleseSungJourney a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Nepalese sung journey"@en, "Nepalesische Gesangsreise"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chant and drum into trance, then describe in largely repetitive song how one leaves the body and the ritual ground and flies with guardian beasts over village, river and mountain passes into the spirit lands and the land of the dead and of the unborn."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Nepalese shamans; it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 64; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAstralProjectionActiveTrance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Astral projection in active trance"@en, "Astralreise im aktiven Zustand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Journeying out of the body without lying deeply relaxed in a quiet place; the live account intensifies perception and lets fellow shamans and audience join in."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 64; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASungJourneyYieldsActiveAstralProjectionYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Sung journey yields active astral projection"@en, "Gesang ergibt Astralreise"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chanting, drumming and sung description produce astral projection and shared participation."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Nepalese shamans; it is entered as his ascription, and the named source is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmANepaleseSungJourney ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmAAstralProjectionActiveTrance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
