pmp:ChaosMagicVmAWalkingTranceExerciseOneWild a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Walking trance (exercise one in the wild)"@en, "Gehtrance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Walk alone for a long time in the countryside, let the rhythmic motion soothe you, coordinate steps with breath, and repeat exercise one while walking, speaking slowly one or two words per breath about body, ground, sounds, light and scenery."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 64; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAPractisePlayfullyTooSeriouslyCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Practise playfully, not too seriously"@en, "Spielerisch üben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Practice is easy in a playful mood and harder when taken too seriously."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmAWalkingTranceExerciseOneWild ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, pp. 65–66 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAMantraWordPerStep a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Mantra word per step"@en, "Mantra pro Schritt"@de ;
    skos:definition "If coordinating breath and steps is hard, choose a suggestive phrase (such as one about learning trance step by step) and say one word per step aloud or mentally."@en ;
    skos:note "Some people report difficulty coordinating breath and steps."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, pp. 65–66 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAFastSpeechWhileWalkingYieldsActiveYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Fast speech while walking yields active trance"@en, "Schnelles Sprechen ergibt aktive Trance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Excited fast speaking during the walk produces the active trance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmAWalkingTranceExerciseOneWild ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmAActivePowerfulWalkingTrance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, pp. 65–66 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAActivePowerfulWalkingTrance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Active powerful walking trance"@en, "Aktive Gehtrance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fast excited speech while walking speeds the pace into a powerful active trance useful for long uphill walking."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, pp. 65–66 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASlowSpeechWhileWalkingYieldsLeisurelyYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Slow speech while walking yields leisurely trance"@en, "Langsames Gehen ergibt Trance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Slowing speech and pace during the walk yields a slow trance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmAWalkingTranceExerciseOneWild ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmASlowLeisurelyTranceTurningInward ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, pp. 65–66 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASlowLeisurelyTranceTurningInward a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Slow leisurely trance turning inward"@en, "Gemächliche Trance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Slowing words, pace and awareness leads to a leisurely trance with the wish to rest, close the eyes and turn inward, which may be followed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, pp. 65–66 (no running head on the page); read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmATenOptionsDeepMindChooses a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ten options, deep mind chooses"@en, "Zehn Möglichkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "In trance, close the eyes and ask the mind’s inventive parts for ten or more activities to enjoy in the trance, good, bad, absurd or impossible; collect ten, then ask the deep mind to pick one and reveal which."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 67; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASeparateInventingJudging a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Separate inventing from judging"@en, "Erfinden und Urteilen trennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creative parts should freely generate choices while other parts judge and select; as in painting, if the critic held the brush nothing would start, hence art schools forbid beginners the eraser."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 67; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmAPouncingFirstOptionAnalysingItDeathFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pouncing on the first option and analysing it to death"@en, "Erste Idee zerreden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Turning inward half-heartedly, seizing the first option and analysing it to shreds leads people to conclude they cannot invent anything; creative parts need time and freedom from interference."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it concerns pmp:ChaosMagicVmATenOptionsDeepMindChooses."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 67; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmAComingOutTrance a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Coming out of trance"@en, "Aus der Trance kommen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reverse the entry: tell yourself you will wake now, give the inner voice a lively, excited tone, breathe deeply several times, stretch, then open the eyes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 67; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmASourcesBandlerGrinderErickson a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sources: Bandler, Grinder, Erickson"@en, "Quellen: Bandler, Grinder, Erickson"@de ;
    skos:definition "For more on sensory channels and hypnotic language patterns the author points to the books of Bandler, Grinder and Milton H. Erickson, indicating the hypnotherapeutic provenance of the chapter’s techniques."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 5 Visualization, p. 68; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

#
# Chapter 6, Access to Imagination
#

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBImaginationBorrowsOuterWorldFormsMore a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Imagination borrows outer-world forms; more senses make it more real"@en, "Vorstellung übernimmt Formen der Außenwelt; mehr Sinne machen sie wirklicher"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagined content takes on sensory shape drawn from the external world; for magick the imagined should be as convincing as possible, and Fries assumes it gains reality the more sensory channels participate."@en ;
    skos:note "Strength in the source: assumption."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 69; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBSensorySpecialisationAndNeedToDevelop a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensory specialisation and the need to develop weak channels"@en, "Sinnesspezialisierung und Ausbildung schwacher Kanäle"@de ;
    skos:definition "People are specialised toward particular sensory modes of thinking (a painter toward pictures, a musician toward sound); the magician has to train the channels in which imagining is hard, and some first have to discover that they already use them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 70; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBHypothesisEveryPresentSenseIsAlso a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hypothesis: every present sense is also used internally"@en, "Hypothese: jeder vorhandene Sinn wird auch innerlich genutzt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working assumption that anyone who has all senses also thinks in all of them, so the visual channel is active even if consciousness fails to notice; the task shifts from creating a new sense to gaining conscious access to an existing one."@en ;
    skos:note "Strength in the source: hypothesis."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 70; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBDirectInstructionToBuildPictureFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Direct instruction to build a picture fails for non-visualisers"@en, "Direkte Anweisung zum Bildaufbau scheitert bei Nicht-Visualisierern"@de ;
    skos:definition "When the friend who could not visualise was simply asked to picture a tree, she tried to assemble an image, could not, and was left feeling incapable and defeated."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of Conscious access to visual imagination; no deadline is set."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 70; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBRecallQuestionsToRevealStoredVisual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Recall questions to reveal stored visual information"@en, "Erinnerungsfragen zum Nachweis gespeicherter Bildinformation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ask questions answerable only from visual memory (how a particular plant looks, where some object stands at home, which route one drives to work); correct answers show that visual data is stored in the deep mind and that only awareness of it is lacking."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 70; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBCrossSensoryInductionOfVisualisation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cross-sensory induction of visualisation"@en, "Kreuzsinnliche Induktion der Visualisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "With the subject’s eyes shut, speak slowly with long pauses. Begin in a channel that works: invite the felt sensation of hands exploring a tree’s bark, its firm solid wood, its roots reaching deep into rich soil. Watch for small bodily cues that the feeling is established, then move to hearing (wind in branches and leaves, calling birds, the wind swaying the tree). Finally remark that the person may notice they have already started seeing the tree inwardly."@en ;
    skos:note "Pattern: lead through an available sense, add a second, and the missing visual channel joins by itself. Fries calls this hypnosis only in the sense in which all storytelling is."@en, "The source orders these steps itself: Author’s sequence: imagined touch first, then hearing, after which sight comes by itself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 70; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBConsciousAccessToVisualImagination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Conscious access to visual imagination"@en, "Bewusster Zugang zur bildhaften Vorstellung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to see imagined content with the inner eye, here gained by a person who had believed she could not visualise anything."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 71; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBBodilyCuesThatImaginedChannelIsSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bodily cues that an imagined channel is established"@en, "Körperzeichen für einen etablierten Vorstellungskanal"@de ;
    skos:definition "The guide judges that the felt tree is in place from small signs: slight hand movements, altered breathing, muscle tone and posture; only then is the next sense added."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of Cross-sensory induction of visualisation; announced to the one practising and judged by the operator."@en, "Operator-observed sign used to pace the induction."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 71; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBCrossSensoryInductionYieldsConsciousAccessTo a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Cross-sensory induction of visualisation yields Conscious access to visual imagination"@en, "Kreuzsinnliche Induktion der Visualisierung ergibt Bewusster Zugang zur bildhaften Vorstellung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practice “Cross-sensory induction of visualisation” is stated to produce “Conscious access to visual imagination”."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmBCrossSensoryInductionOfVisualisation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmBConsciousAccessToVisualImagination ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 71; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBVisionArrivedUnpromptedBeforeItWasOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Vision arrived unprompted before it was named"@en, "Bild erschien von selbst, bevor es benannt wurde"@de ;
    skos:definition "By the time hearing had been added the friend was already seeing, naturally and well before the speaker mentioned sight."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report: of Cross-sensory induction of visualisation; reported after the fact, not announced in advance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 71; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBReadingAndStorytellingAsTranceAnd a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reading and storytelling as trance and hypnosis"@en, "Lesen und Erzählen als Trance und Hypnose"@de ;
    skos:definition "Everyone who narrates, writes or describes uses hypnosis in the plain sense: words are empty and hearers or readers must hallucinate meaning into them; absorbed reading, with the body nearly idle for hours, is itself a trance state."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 71; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBBuildingFullMultisensoryRepresentation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Building a full multisensory representation"@en, "Aufbau einer vollständigen mehrsinnlichen Darstellung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choose an imagined scene such as a stream and test each sense in turn: the sound of the water, its cold, the pull of the current, damp air, its taste, the smell of rotting plants at the bank, the sight of waves and foam. Enter whichever senses come easily, strengthen them by describing them aloud, and build a complete representation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 72; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBStrengthenedMultisensoryImagination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Strengthened multisensory imagination"@en, "Gestärkte mehrsinnliche Vorstellungskraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagination that is vivid across several senses and so convincing enough for magical work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 72; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBBuildingFullMultisensoryYieldsStrengthenedMultisensoryImagination a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Building a full multisensory representation yields Strengthened multisensory imagination"@en, "Aufbau einer vollständigen mehrsinnlichen Darstellung ergibt Gestärkte mehrsinnliche Vorstellungskraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practice “Building a full multisensory representation” is stated to produce “Strengthened multisensory imagination”."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmBBuildingFullMultisensoryRepresentation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmBStrengthenedMultisensoryImagination ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 72; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBBuildingFullMultisensoryYieldsAutomatisedImaginingLearned a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Building a full multisensory representation yields Automatised imagining learned by the deep mind"@en, "Aufbau einer vollständigen mehrsinnlichen Darstellung ergibt Vom Tiefengeist erlerntes automatisches Vorstellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practice “Building a full multisensory representation” is stated to produce “Automatised imagining learned by the deep mind”."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmBBuildingFullMultisensoryRepresentation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAutomatisedImaginingLearnedByDeepMind ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 72; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBPracticeMakesImaginingEasyThenNaturalSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Practice makes imagining easy, then natural, then automatic"@en, "Übung macht Vorstellen leicht, natürlich, automatisch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced progression: with some practice the method becomes easy, with more persistence it feels natural, and soon it happens automatically."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of Building a full multisensory representation; announced to the one practising and judged by the operator."@en, "Series: easy, natural, automatic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 72; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAutomatisedImaginingLearnedByDeepMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Automatised imagining learned by the deep mind"@en, "Vom Tiefengeist erlerntes automatisches Vorstellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once the deep mind has learned the process, imagining runs by itself and the conscious mind is free for new learning."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 72; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBPaleShallowOrDiffuseVisionsFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pale, shallow or diffuse visions"@en, "Blasse, flache oder diffuse Visionen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A frequent complaint: people do see inwardly, but the image lacks strength, depth or definition."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of Strengthened multisensory imagination; no deadline is set."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 72; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAstralProjectionAsTravelThroughDeep a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Astral projection as travel through the deep mind"@en, "Astralprojektion als Reise durch den Tiefengeist"@de ;
    skos:definition "In astral projection the traveller crosses an imagined dream world in a body that is likewise imagined (human or alien); that world is made and kept up by the deep mind, so the traveller is in effect journeying through the deep mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 72; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBAstralDoorwayEntry a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Astral doorway entry"@en, "Eintritt durch die astrale Pforte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagine a doorway, gate or entrance in great detail, how it looks and how it feels, and invest much time in making it real. Then picture yourself in front of it, open it and step into the world beyond. Study its setting (what the frame joins onto, what the ground is) and let a whole reality grow from small details; move through it at leisure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 72; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAstralDoorwayEntryYieldsAstralTravelIn a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Astral doorway entry yields Astral travel in imagined worlds"@en, "Eintritt durch die astrale Pforte ergibt Astralreise in vorgestellten Welten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practice “Astral doorway entry” is stated to produce “Astral travel in imagined worlds”."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmBAstralDoorwayEntry ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAstralTravelInImaginedWorlds ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 72; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBImaginedWorldsGrowMoreRealWhen a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Imagined worlds grow more real when explored"@en, "Vorgestellte Welten werden durch Erkunden wirklicher"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imaginary worlds gain reality as one explores them, and slow movement through them attunes the traveller to the deep-mind regions they represent; a whole world can unfold from tiny details."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAstralTravelInImaginedWorlds a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Astral travel in imagined worlds"@en, "Astralreise in vorgestellten Welten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Entering and exploring dream worlds, and through them coming into tune with the deep-mind regions those worlds represent."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBMemoryRouteDrawingSymbolToRecall a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Memory route: drawing a symbol to recall it"@en, "Erinnerungsweg: Symbol zeichnen, um es abzurufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To visualise a sigil or symbol (for example blazing, traced by the wand in fiery lines), first draw or paint it large on paper and study it as long as needed; afterwards it is not built up inwardly but simply remembered."@en ;
    skos:note "Many who cannot construct images can still recall them easily."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBVividVisualisationOfSigilOrSymbol a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Vivid visualisation of a sigil or symbol"@en, "Lebhafte Visualisierung von Sigille oder Symbol"@de ;
    skos:definition "Holding a radiant symbol in the imagination, e.g. as lines of fire drawn with the wand."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBMemoryRouteDrawingYieldsVividVisualisationOf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Memory route: drawing a symbol to recall it yields Vivid visualisation of a sigil or symbol"@en, "Erinnerungsweg: Symbol zeichnen, um es abzurufen ergibt Lebhafte Visualisierung von Sigille oder Symbol"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practice “Memory route: drawing a symbol to recall it” is stated to produce “Vivid visualisation of a sigil or symbol”."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmBMemoryRouteDrawingSymbolToRecall ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmBVividVisualisationOfSigilOrSymbol ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBGodFormDefined a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "God-form defined"@en, "Gottesform bestimmt"@de ;
    skos:definition "A god-form is the image of a deity one wants to contact; the remembering technique is used to build it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBBuildingAndAnimatingGodForm a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Building and animating a god-form"@en, "Aufbau und Belebung einer Gottesform"@de ;
    skos:definition "Study the chosen deity: read every myth and legend available, paint pictures of it, learn which aspects of nature, energies and states of awareness belong to it. Meditate on the picture’s shape, colours, posture and attributes, either by gazing at it with mind emptied or through speech, calls, invoking or music; this releases emotional energy which the picture gathers. Then pass from the painted image to the remembered inner one and build a solid representation. Call the deity by prayer or invocation until, once attuned, the current flows and the image comes alive. When accustomed, merge with the god, take on its form and let it indwell, inspire and obsess you."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBStudyingGodLore a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Studying the god's lore"@en, "Studium der Überlieferung des Gottes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Begin by reading every myth and legend of the chosen deity that can be found, and by working out which aspects of nature it stands for and which energies and states of awareness belong to it."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the six-stage series of god-form work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBPaintingGodForm a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Painting the god-form"@en, "Malen der Gottesform"@de ;
    skos:definition "Paint a picture of the deity, whatever one's skill, after looking closely at the images tradition has made of it, so that its form is really seen."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the six-stage series of god-form work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBChargedMeditationOnPaintedImage a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Charged meditation on the painted image"@en, "Geladene Meditation über das gemalte Bild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Direct awareness at the picture: contemplate its form, colours, posture and attributes, staring with an empty mind or speaking, calling, invoking or making music, so that the emotional energy released gathers in the picture."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the six-stage series of god-form work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBStagesOfGodFormWorkStages a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Stages of god-form work"@en, "Stufen der Gottesform-Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sequence given in the text: study of lore, painting, charged meditation on the picture, inner recall, invocation, union."@en ;
    skos:note "The series of the steps of pmp:ChaosMagicVmBBuildingAndAnimatingGodForm."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:ChaosMagicVmBStudyingGodLore ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:ChaosMagicVmBPaintingGodForm ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:ChaosMagicVmBChargedMeditationOnPaintedImage ;
    rdf:_4 pmp:ChaosMagicVmBRecallingGodFormInwardly ;
    rdf:_5 pmp:ChaosMagicVmBInvokingGodIntoItsInnerImage ;
    rdf:_6 pmc:ChaosMagicVmBUnionWithAndPossessionByGod ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Fries gives god-form work as a sequence in which each stage feeds the next: the lore studied and the deity painted give the picture its exactness, the charged meditation stores emotional energy in it, the inner recall carries it into the imagination, invocation brings it alive there, and only one used to the living contact is invited to merge with the god." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBRecallingGodFormInwardly a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Recalling the god-form inwardly"@en, "Inneres Erinnern der Gottesform"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pass from the material picture to the inner one: remember how the painting looks and build from that memory a solid representation of the god in the imagination."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the six-stage series of god-form work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBPaintingForcesCloseSeeingSkillIrrelevant a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Painting forces close seeing; skill irrelevant"@en, "Malen erzwingt genaues Sehen; Können unerheblich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Painting ability does not matter; painting the god demands close study of all traditional images, which guarantees that the form is really seen, however odd one’s own picture turns out."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBBuildingAndAnimatingYieldsLivingContactWith a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Building and animating a god-form yields Living contact with a deity through its image"@en, "Aufbau und Belebung einer Gottesform ergibt Lebendiger Kontakt mit einer Gottheit über ihr Bild"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practice “Building and animating a god-form” is stated to produce “Living contact with a deity through its image”."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmBBuildingAndAnimatingGodForm ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmBLivingContactWithDeityThroughIts ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBInvokingGodIntoItsInnerImage a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Invoking the god into its inner image"@en, "Anrufung des Gottes in sein inneres Bild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Call to the deity with prayer or invocation until, attuned to its nature, one finds the current flowing and the image coming alive, the sentience having received a body to appear in."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the six-stage series of god-form work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73-75; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBLivingContactWithDeityThroughIts a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Living contact with a deity through its image"@en, "Lebendiger Kontakt mit einer Gottheit über ihr Bild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once attuned, the current flows and the image animates because the deity’s sentience has been given a body to manifest in; the picture becomes a channel through which divine sentience reaches the practitioner."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 73; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBFamiliarityWithContactBeforeMergingPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Familiarity with the contact before merging"@en, "Vertrautheit mit dem Kontakt vor der Vereinigung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Merging and possession are offered only after one has grown used to the living contact."@en ;
    skos:note "No consequence of skipping is stated."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmBLivingContactWithDeityThroughIts ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmBUnionWithAndPossessionByGod ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 75; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBUnionWithAndPossessionByGod a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Union with and possession by a god"@en, "Vereinigung mit und Besessenheit durch einen Gott"@de ;
    skos:definition "Merging with the god, assuming its form and being indwelt, inspired and obsessed by it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 75; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBBuildingAndAnimatingYieldsUnionWithAnd a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Building and animating a god-form yields Union with and possession by a god"@en, "Aufbau und Belebung einer Gottesform ergibt Vereinigung mit und Besessenheit durch einen Gott"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practice “Building and animating a god-form” is stated to produce “Union with and possession by a god”."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmBBuildingAndAnimatingGodForm ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmBUnionWithAndPossessionByGod ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 75; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBPictureIsLinkNotGod a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The picture is a link, not the god"@en, "Das Bild ist Bindeglied, nicht der Gott"@de ;
    skos:definition "The painted image, good or bad, joins a traditional form to an imagined one; it is not the deity but a connection through which divine sentience may touch us."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 75; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAnthropomorphicGodImagesAsMasks a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Anthropomorphic god-images as masks"@en, "Menschengestaltige Götterbilder als Masken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Human-shaped images of gods are conventions that make identification and union with natural forces easier; one should keep in mind that they are masks."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 75; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBLokiFireGodNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Loki as fire-god"@en, "Loki als Feuergott"@de ;
    skos:definition "Loki is treated as a fire deity, in essence flame, with whom communication and union are easier through a human-shaped form; referred to as her/him."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Loki" ;
    pm:nameRole "fire-god, force of nature" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 75; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBMonotheismUnbalancesMagiciansWorkSeveralGodCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Monotheism unbalances magicians; work several god-forms"@en, "Monotheismus macht Magier einseitig; mehrere Gottesformen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever works with god-forms should invoke several, since exclusive devotion to one deity yields badly unbalanced magicians."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmBBuildingAndAnimatingGodForm ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 75; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBEachGodLinksToHiddenAspect a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Each god links to a hidden aspect of self"@en, "Jeder Gott verbindet mit einem verborgenen Selbstaspekt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every god contacted connects with some further aspect of one’s being that had been subconscious until then."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 75; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBCongruenceWithInvokedGod a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Congruence with the invoked god"@en, "Kongruenz mit dem angerufenen Gott"@de ;
    skos:definition "The magician must match the god being invoked: one has to resemble the gods one wants to discover within."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
