pmc:ChaosMagicVmBHealthierDevelopedAggression a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healthier, developed aggression"@en, "Entwickelte, gesündere Aggression"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once fierce enough to be real to Mars, the contacted part of oneself shows many ways of being more aggressive, and in healthier ways."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 75; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAnubisNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Anubis (Anpu)"@en, "Anubis (Anpu)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Jackal god who journeys through gates and passages and bears the dead to the otherworld; the author’s first god-form; called Anubis of the desert waste, with eyes of Sothis fire."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Anubis", "Anpu" ;
    pm:nameRole "jackal god, guide of the dead, guardian of passages" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 76; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBChargingAndEnhancingPaintedGodImage a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Charging and enhancing a painted god image (Anubis working)"@en, "Laden und Steigern eines gemalten Götterbildes (Anubis-Arbeit)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Paint a stele of the god in traditional style (here Anpu seated, in Egyptian profile); charge it through a period of invocation and ceremony with passion and power; then recall the picture at every spare moment as clearly as possible and make the inner image more attractive than the painted one: enlarge it, bring it nearer, add luminous colour, try sharp contrast, radiance, sparkle or soft glow, shift the viewpoint (below, beside, above), and add wonder and an inner voice that sings and chants the god’s names."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 76; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBImagePulsingWithVitalitySign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Image pulsing with vitality"@en, "Bild pulsiert vor Lebendigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: with these enhancements the inner image soon throbs with life."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of Charging and enhancing a painted god image (Anubis working); announced to the one practising and judged by the operator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 76; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAnubisCameAliveOnTrainOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Anubis came alive on a train"@en, "Anubis wurde im Zug lebendig"@de ;
    skos:definition "About ten years before writing, in his first god-form work, the vivid image suddenly took over while Fries sat in a train: the jackal god turned his head and stared at him with eyes burning in frozen Sothis fire, his body shook and he broke into sweat."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report: of Charging and enhancing a painted god image (Anubis working); reported after the fact, not announced in advance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 76; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBLustOfResultBlocksBreakthroughFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lust of result blocks the breakthrough"@en, "Lust am Ergebnis blockiert den Durchbruch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Implied failure condition: in a temple the practitioner strains for results; the breakthrough came on a train, where such striving was minimal."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of Living contact with a deity through its image; no deadline is set."@en, "Strength in the source: implied (we may assume)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 76; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBImageMagicModelImageEnergyAwakening a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Image magic model: image, energy, awakening"@en, "Modell der Bildmagie: Bild, Energie, Erwachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In spell-crafting, shape-changing, astral projection, god-, beast- and tree-forms and some kinds of divination one first creates an image; charged with fitting energy and sentience it becomes a message that touches something deep; the relevant parts of the deep mind then wake and animate it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 76; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBCreatingImage a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating the image"@en, "Erschaffen des Bildes"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first stage shared by astral travel, work with god-, beast- and tree-forms, spell-crafting, changing shape and some divination: the conscious mind builds an image and spends much time and care making it detailed, solid and convincing."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the three-stage series of image magic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 76; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBThreeStagesOfImageMagicStages a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Three stages of image magic"@en, "Drei Stufen der Bildmagie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Create the image; fill it with energy and sentience; the deep mind awakens it."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:ChaosMagicVmBCreatingImage ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:ChaosMagicVmBEnergySuppliesForAnimatingImages ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAwakeningOfImageByDeepMind ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Fries names three stages common to all image work: an image is built by the conscious mind, then charged with energy and sentience from the listed supplies, and only then woken by the deep mind; the third has no object without the first two." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 76; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBEnergySuppliesForAnimatingImages a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Energy supplies for animating images"@en, "Energiequellen zur Belebung von Bildern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Listed sources: prayer, invocation, religious belief, deep longing, song, mantra, sex, chanting, dance, offering one’s energy or bodily secretions, and sacrificing flowers, food or blood."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 76; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAwakeningOfImageByDeepMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Awakening of the image by the deep mind"@en, "Erweckung des Bildes durch den Tiefengeist"@de ;
    skos:definition "The third stage of image magic: once the image has been charged with fitting energy and sentience, whatever deep-mind regions it reaches wake up and bring it to life, in ways the conscious mind cannot foresee."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the three-stage series of image magic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 76-77; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBConsciousMindCannotPredictDeepMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Conscious mind cannot predict deep-mind activity"@en, "Bewusstsein kann Tiefengeist-Tätigkeit nicht vorhersagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "What the deep mind does when it uses an image as a channel differs greatly from what the conscious mind imagines."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 77; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBStatusOfGodsLeftOpenFor a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Status of the gods left open for practice"@en, "Status der Götter für die Praxis offen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gods are independent of the ego; they may also be viewed as natural forces whose human shapes are conventions (calling a sun deity male or female mirrors cultural gender beliefs), or as deep-mind parts unrecognised by the ego. Since they manifest through our senses and nervous system, one cannot settle whether they belong to that system or contact us through it, and may answer as convenient."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 77; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBUniversalConnectionOfAllSelf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Universal connection of all self"@en, "Alles Selbst hängt mit allem Selbst zusammen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gods, ghosts, spirits, demons, angels and totems are best treated as convenient forms for communicating with aspects of oneself and of all-self, whatever they ultimately are."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 77; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBDoNotTakeWishfulThinkingForCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not take wishful thinking for a spirit"@en, "Wunschdenken nicht für einen Geist halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beware of accepting any wishful fantasy as a genuine spiritual manifestation; spirits may and ought to be put to the test, as Crowley repeatedly stressed."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries ascribes this to Aleister Crowley; the named source is reachable in its own right and is not read through him, so the node is entered as his ascription and not as a mediated reading."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmBLivingContactWithDeityThroughIts ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 77; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBDiscerningGenuineSpiritsFromWishfulThinking a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Discerning genuine spirits from wishful thinking"@en, "Unterscheidung echter Geister von Wunschdenken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Judging whether a perceived being stems from forces beyond the ego or from one’s own wishes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 77; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBTestingSpiritByEgosReaction a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Testing a spirit by the ego’s reaction"@en, "Geisterprüfung an der Reaktion des Ego"@de ;
    skos:definition "To judge whether a god or animal spirit is real (driven by force and awareness beyond the ego), watch how the ego responds: whether it inflates or grows uneasy, and whether something new is learned."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 77; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBTestingSpiritByYieldsDiscerningGenuineSpirits a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Testing a spirit by the ego’s reaction yields Discerning genuine spirits from wishful thinking"@en, "Geisterprüfung an der Reaktion des Ego ergibt Unterscheidung echter Geister von Wunschdenken"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practice “Testing a spirit by the ego’s reaction” is stated to produce “Discerning genuine spirits from wishful thinking”."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmBTestingSpiritByEgosReaction ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmBDiscerningGenuineSpiritsFromWishfulThinking ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 77; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBInflatedEgoMarksWishfulThinkingSpiritFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inflated ego marks a wishful-thinking spirit"@en, "Aufgeblähtes Ego kennzeichnet Wunschgeist"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the ego swells with pride, grandiosity or the usual lukewarm cosmic wisdom, the perceived being is very likely a product of wishful thinking."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of Living contact with a deity through its image; no deadline is set."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 77; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBUnpredictableImageryAndEgoUneaseAsSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unpredictable imagery and ego unease as signs of a real being"@en, "Unvorhersehbare Bilder und Unbehagen des Ego als Zeichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagination transforming in unforeseen ways and the ego feeling uneasy or upset indicate the evoked being is stronger than the ego; real spirits transform the ego as part of their task, so it naturally feels queasy."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of Testing a spirit by the ego’s reaction; announced to the one practising and judged by the operator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 78; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBLearningSomethingNewAndUsefulAsSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Learning something new and useful as sign"@en, "Neues und Nützliches lernen als Zeichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A further good sign: one learns something new and useful and discovers aspects of oneself that were unknown or problematic."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of Testing a spirit by the ego’s reaction; announced to the one practising and judged by the operator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 78; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBNoObjectiveProofOfSpirits a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No objective proof of spirits"@en, "Kein objektiver Beweis für Geister"@de ;
    skos:definition "These signs offer no objective proof, only assurance that something beneficial is going on."@en ;
    skos:note "A statement on how far the method can be tested: no objective proof, only signs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
