pmc:ChaosMagicVmBDeepMindUpheavalNeedsCopingMethodCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Deep-mind upheaval needs a coping method"@en, "Aufruhr aus dem Tiefengeist braucht eine Bewältigungsmethode"@de ;
    skos:definition "Consciously built visions are comparatively safe; once the deep mind unfolds into awareness, releasing anything from pure inspiration to repressed and forgotten horrors, a sound method for handling the turmoil may be required."@en ;
    skos:note "The caution is about image work in general, at the point where the deep mind starts answering the consciously built image."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmBImageMagicModelImageEnergyAwakening ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 78; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAgainstAncientDemonisingOfPainfulMaterialDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the ancient demonising of painful material"@en, "Gegen die antike Dämonisierung schmerzhaften Materials"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mages of antiquity labelled painful inner material demonic instead of healing and integrating it, and built a model of warring good and bad forces with the ego as sole judge; Fries rejects this."@en ;
    skos:note "Dispute read from one side only: Fries against mages of antiquity; the other side is not read here, so the node is a pm:Conceptualizing and not a pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 78; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBEvenWorstInnerDemonServesWhole a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Even the worst inner demon serves the whole system"@en, "Auch der schlimmste innere Dämon dient dem Ganzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dangerous visions are released with good intent: the deep mind presents horrid images so that one may learn to accept and deal with them, and there are methods to handle such material without being swamped."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 78; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBBanishing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Banishing"@en, "Bannen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ritual practice for removing or controlling dangerous material; in ritual it clears everyday worries and disturbing thoughts, in astral work the awareness of body and surroundings, in god-form work one’s human identity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 78; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBBanishBeforeInvokingPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Banish before invoking"@en, "Erst bannen, dann anrufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In ritual, astral projection and god-form work alike, banishing comes first and invocation follows."@en ;
    skos:note "No consequence of skipping is stated."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmBBanishing ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmBInvocation ;
