pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAssociatedVersusDissociatedAwareness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Associated versus dissociated awareness"@en, "Assoziierte versus dissoziierte Wahrnehmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any vision, built or remembered, can be perceived associated (inside the scene, through one’s own eyes, ears and body, as if now) or dissociated (watching oneself in the scene from some outside viewpoint); the choice affects experience more than one realises."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries ascribes this to Neuro-Linguistic Programming (NLP); the named source is reachable in its own right and is not read through him, so the node is entered as his ascription and not as a mediated reading."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 79; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBMemoriesAreConstructsPerspectiveIsAdjustable a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Memories are constructs; perspective is adjustable"@en, "Erinnerungen sind Konstrukte; Perspektive ist wählbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "The objection that association is more real is dubious: memories are constructions, and the viewpoint can be switched so that memories and visions become easier to recall and handle."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 79; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBDissociatingUnpleasantMemory a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dissociating an unpleasant memory (cinema technique)"@en, "Dissoziieren einer unangenehmen Erinnerung (Kinotechnik)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pick a mildly unpleasant memory, nothing traumatic. Notice how you recall it (from inside or outside). First associate and relive it as if happening now. After recovering, repeat dissociated: take a seat at the rear of a cinema, the lights dim, the curtain opens, and you watch yourself act on the screen. Ease it further by moving the screen away, shrinking it, paling the colours, switching to black and white, altering speed or adding another soundtrack. Experiment until the whole event can be recalled without distress."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries ascribes this to NLP exercise (Exercise two); the named source is reachable in its own right and is not read through him, so the node is entered as his ascription and not as a mediated reading."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 79; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBStartWithNothingTraumaticCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Start with nothing traumatic"@en, "Nicht mit Traumatischem beginnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "For the first trials use only a moderately unpleasant scene, not a trauma."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmBDissociatingUnpleasantMemory ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 79; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBReluctanceToRememberMarksRightMaterialSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reluctance to remember marks the right material"@en, "Widerwille gegen Erinnern zeigt das richtige Material"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not wanting to recall the scene is an excellent sign that suitable material has been chosen."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of Dissociating an unpleasant memory (cinema technique); announced to the one practising and judged by the operator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 79; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBSceneEasierToBearWhenDissociatedSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Scene easier to bear when dissociated"@en, "Szene dissoziiert leichter erträglich"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the screened version is easier to cope with, one is on the right track."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of Dissociating an unpleasant memory (cinema technique); announced to the one practising and judged by the operator."@en ;
