pmc:ChaosMagicVmBDissociationIsNotRepressionCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Dissociation is not repression"@en, "Dissoziation ist keine Verdrängung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dissociating awful memories means separating out the bad feelings, not suppressing the experience; even dreadful memories carry valuable information to keep available. Bandler is credited with showing that the pattern can be learned."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries ascribes this to Richard Bandler; the named source is reachable in its own right and is not read through him, so the node is entered as his ascription and not as a mediated reading."@en ;
