pmc:ChaosMagicVmBDecisionsArePreparedByDeepMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Decisions are prepared by the deep mind through representation"@en, "Entscheidungen werden vom Tiefengeist über Darstellung vorbereitet"@de ;
    skos:definition "At a forest crossroads Fries found that the mountain option had been shown as a distant, misty, gloomy view of a tiny figure on a pointless path, the meadow option as a close, rich, associated sensory scene; the deep mind had made one choice far more attractive, and the conscious mind merely believed it chose."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 83; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBExaminingHowOneRepresentsChoices a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Examining how one represents choices"@en, "Untersuchen, wie man Wahlmöglichkeiten darstellt"@de ;
    skos:definition "At the next decision, however minor, stop and go back mentally to inspect how each option was presented: the inner picture, any inner speech, and the feeling that tipped the balance; check whether the decision was in fact made long before."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 84; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

