pmp:ChaosMagicVmBMutationalLeapFromPointToPoint a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Mutational leap from point A to point B"@en, "Mutationssprung von Punkt A zu Punkt B"@de ;
    skos:definition "For stuck, morbid brooding: (1) recognise you want to change your mind; (2) stop what you were doing; this spot is point A; (3) associate with your inner state: thoughts, feelings, inner images, inner voice, mood, muscle tone, posture, breathing; (4) turn attention outward and, without moving, build a representation of surroundings, scenery and weather; (5) spin round and leap backward; (6) from this point B, picture yourself still standing at A as you looked a moment ago; (7) improve that dissociated image: better posture, freer breath, relaxed muscles, a changed expression, a radiant coloured aura, and for entering a magical world surround it with ghosts, gods and spirits, until it is clear, vivid and attractive; (8) once it is stable, breathe deeply, spin and leap forward into point A and into the image; (9) become it and walk off briskly into the new world."@en ;
    skos:note "The source orders these steps itself: Numbered sequence from recognising the wish to change, through inner and outer sensing, the backward leap and improving the image, to leaping forward into it and walking on."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 85; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBImageEstablishedBeforeForwardLeapPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Image established before the forward leap"@en, "Bild gefestigt vor dem Vorwärtssprung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The leap into the image follows only once the improved vision is firmly in place."@en ;
    skos:note "The prior step is step 7 of the leap, improving the dissociated image."@en, "No consequence of skipping is stated."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmBMutationalLeapFromPointToPoint ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAccessToNewStateOfMind ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 86; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

