pmc:ChaosMagicVmBColourChangesMeaningChooseCongruentColours a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Colour changes meaning; choose congruent colours"@en, "Farbe verändert Bedeutung; kongruente Farben wählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Abstract energies are imagined as coloured fields, currents or rays; colouring light alters its meaning, and colours painted on rooms, symbols, stelae or sigils should match the forces and states one wills to invoke."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 87; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAgainstBookishColourCorrespondenceTablesDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against bookish colour-correspondence tables"@en, "Gegen buchgelehrte Farbentsprechungstabellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The usual intellectual method, where the word-bound mage studies the literature and adopts a traditional correspondence list meant to suit everyone, has the conscious mind guessing what something means to the deep mind; with great luck it is nearly right."@en ;
    skos:note "Dispute read from one side only: Fries against traditional correspondence lists of magical and psychological literature; the other side is not read here, so the node is a pm:Conceptualizing and not a pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 87; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBSharedAndDifferingColourMeanings a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shared and differing colour meanings"@en, "Gemeinsame und abweichende Farbbedeutungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some meanings are nearly universal (light versus dark, red and blood, white and age); others vary with preference, personal history (fear of drowning spoils ocean blue-green), intensity and culture (in China white is worn for mourning and a white blossom in the hair is unlucky; some Eastern religions picture the void as white)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 87; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBProbingColourIntensityThresholds a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Probing colour intensity thresholds"@en, "Erkunden von Farbintensitätsschwellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Surround yourself with a sphere of pure white light and brighten it, looking for the point where it becomes unpleasant; take a pleasant colour and raise its intensity to the point of being overwhelmed; or start bright and dim it; observe how awareness and emotional response shift; do the same with a memory, saturating its colours or letting them fade."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 88; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

