    rdfs:label "Probing colour intensity thresholds yields Knowing what colours mean to oneself"@en, "Erkunden von Farbintensitätsschwellen ergibt Wissen, was Farben einem selbst bedeuten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practice “Probing colour intensity thresholds” is stated to produce “Knowing what colours mean to oneself”."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmBProbingColourIntensityThresholds ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmBKnowingWhatColoursMeanToOneself ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 88; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAgainstPositiveThinkingWhiteLightHealingDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against positive-thinking white-light healing"@en, "Gegen Weißlicht-Heilung des positiven Denkens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fries mocks the healing white light marketed by innumerable positive thinkers to their followers in Europe and America as culturally blind."@en ;
    skos:note "Dispute read from one side only: Fries against positive-thinking teachers; the other side is not read here, so the node is a pm:Conceptualizing and not a pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 88; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBWhiteLightHealingCanHarmWhereCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "White-light healing can harm where white means death"@en, "Weißlicht-Heilung kann schaden, wo Weiß Tod bedeutet"@de ;
    skos:definition "The white-light healing sold to followers might seriously upset a Chinese person whose deep mind ties white to death and emptiness; white light heals only if white means healing to that person."@en ;
    skos:note "The caution is about the white-light healing of the positive thinkers that the dispute node describes."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAgainstPositiveThinkingWhiteLightHealingDispute ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 88; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBKnowingWhatColoursMeanToOneself a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing what colours mean to oneself"@en, "Wissen, was Farben einem selbst bedeuten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Personal knowledge of one’s own colour meanings and responses, usable in magick and daily life."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 88; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAgainstOldAeonMastersFixingColourDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against old-aeon masters fixing colour codes"@en, "Gegen Meister des alten Äons, die Farbcodes festlegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the old aeon a master settled what colours meant and assumed it valid for all; only followers with similar minds succeeded and the rest were blamed; what they needed was a tradition in which everyone develops their own methods."@en ;
    skos:note "Dispute read from one side only: Fries against master-centred esoteric tradition of the old aeon; the other side is not read here, so the node is a pm:Conceptualizing and not a pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 88; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBBorrowedColourCodeFailsForUnlikeFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Borrowed colour code fails for unlike minds"@en, "Übernommener Farbcode versagt bei andersartigem Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Followers whose minds did not resemble the master’s could not make his colour scheme work and were told the fault was their own."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of Knowing what colours mean to oneself; no deadline is set."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 89; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBFiveColourExperimentsScheme a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Five colour experiments"@en, "Fünf Farbexperimente"@de ;
    skos:definition "Exercise three: immersion, curtain journey, recoloured memories, daily-life aura, fine shades."@en ;
    skos:note "An author-made scheme: Fries's own ordering for this book, not a series whose members take their sense from their place."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Jan Fries, in Visual Magick" ;
