pmp:ChaosMagicVmBColourImmersionInLightTrance a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Colour immersion in light trance"@en, "Farbeintauchen in leichter Trance"@de ;
    skos:definition "For those who imagine colours easily: get comfortable and enter a gentle, relaxed trance; picture a colour, concentrate on it, talk about it with the inner voice, feel it as having substance, texture and density, and let it surround you as vividly as possible; note reactions, ideas, feelings and emotions and where they could serve; when done, let it evaporate, breathe deeply and open the eyes, which closes the unit like a ritual bell; shut them again for the next colour."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 89; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

