pmp:ChaosMagicVmBColourCurtainDoorwayJourney a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Colour-curtain doorway journey"@en, "Reise durch den Farbvorhang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Astral style: imagine standing before a doorway hung with a heavy cloth curtain in the colour to be studied; take time to look at it, feel the cloth, hear yourself speak of the colour; tell yourself a whole world in that colour lies behind it; when ready, open it and go through, perhaps through several doors and curtains, into the world the deep mind made to show the colour’s meaning; once enough has been learned, come back by the same route."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 6 Access to Imagination, p. 89; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

