#
# Chapter 7, Imagination and Prayer
#

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBVoiceModulationChangesExperience a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Voice modulation changes experience"@en, "Stimmmodulation verändert Erleben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moving attention between sensory channels changes awareness, and the tempo, rhythm and emphasis with which one speaks of an experience alter it, opening many states of consciousness; our culture attends to word meaning and wastes the information carried by modulation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 91; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBTwoKindsOfInformationInSpeech a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two kinds of information in speech: what and how"@en, "Zwei Informationsarten in der Rede: Was und Wie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Brain research is cited: regions mostly in the left hemisphere grasp word meaning, regions of the other respond to tempo, modulation and energy; in many people this split lines up with conscious and unconscious functioning, and most attend to content (the what) while ignoring manner (the how)."@en ;
    skos:note "Strength in the source: studies indicate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 91; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBInvocationTreatedLikeReasonedDiscussionFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Invocation treated like a reasoned discussion"@en, "Anrufung wie eine vernünftige Diskussion behandelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "A common mistake: insisting on perfect wording and genuine names of power makes speaking so hard that the invocation falters."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of Invocation; no deadline is set."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 92; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBWritingAndMemorisingInvocations a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Writing and memorising invocations"@en, "Anrufungen schreiben und auswendig lernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Where perfectionism makes free speech difficult, compose invocations beforehand and learn them by heart (unless a classical prayer is used)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 92; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAgainstDoctrineOfTrueSecretGodDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the doctrine of true secret god-names"@en, "Gegen die Lehre der wahren geheimen Götternamen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fries ridicules witches who claim that only traditional, secret, true god-names give genuine contact, and young Wiccans reciting long name lists they barely understand in order to raise power."@en ;
    skos:note "Dispute read from one side only: Fries against some witches; young Wiccans; the other side is not read here, so the node is a pm:Conceptualizing and not a pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 92; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBCorrectInvocationInDullVoiceAchievesFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Correct invocation in a dull voice achieves little"@en, "Richtige Anrufung mit stumpfer Stimme bewirkt wenig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even with the right meaning, an invocation delivered with dull or everyday modulation achieves little."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of Invocation; no deadline is set."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 92; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBGoldenDawnVibrationOfWords a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Golden Dawn vibration of words"@en, "Vibrieren der Worte (Golden Dawn)"@de ;
    skos:definition "To enter the mood, first recite what builds self-confidence (names, titles, achievements); then deliver the invocation in a sonorous, dramatic voice that seems to shake the earth and carry to the edge of the universe."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries ascribes this to the Golden Dawn; the named source is reachable in its own right and is not read through him, so the node is entered as his ascription and not as a mediated reading."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 92; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

