pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAlexSandersAndOneTechniqueMageDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Alex Sanders and the one-technique mage"@en, "Alex Sanders und der Magier mit nur einer Technik"@de ;
    skos:definition "On a tape of Alex Sanders, self-proclaimed witch king, Fries found the first ten minutes dramatic, was bored after fifteen, and after twenty heard the spirit of Loki mocking those who learn one working technique and never another; most mages, he says, stop at the dramatic voice."@en ;
    skos:note "Dispute read from one side only: Fries against Alex Sanders; most ceremonial mages; the other side is not read here, so the node is a pm:Conceptualizing and not a pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 92; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBLokiInnerMockingCriticNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Loki as inner mocking critic"@en, "Loki als innerer Spötter"@de ;
    skos:definition "The spirit of Loki speaks in the author’s deep mind with snide remarks about one-technique magicians."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Loki" ;
    pm:nameRole "trickster spirit voice in the deep mind" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
