pmc:ChaosMagicVmBEmphasisingHowChaosLanguageAndBarbarous a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Emphasising the how: chaos language and barbarous names"@en, "Betonung des Wie: Chaossprache und barbarische Namen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enochian calls, barbarous names and chanting in chaos language direct attention to sound, volume and modulation; meaningless to consciousness, they compensate with power; beginners’ unease reveals the ego’s compulsive need for control."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 93; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

