pmc:ChaosMagicVmBWhatToInvokeElementsOrAny a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "What to invoke: elements or any forces"@en, "Was anrufen: Elemente oder beliebige Kräfte"@de ;
    skos:definition "One may call the four (or five) elements, planetary forces, the sephiroth, favourite god-forms or any suitable being; in Africa, Fries adds, mages invoke the gods and spirits they personally deal with rather than the elements."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 96; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBInvokingElementsInThreeSpeechStages a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Invoking the elements in three speech stages"@en, "Anrufung der Elemente in drei Redestufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Speak aloud, starting with earth: first describe what you call (its qualities, places, colours, weight, the patience of stones); second, affirm unity with it (feel it in the land and in your own flesh and bones); third, speak as the element itself in the first person. Draw material from memories of the element. When imagination is vivid, pour it into the fluid until it brims with the element’s qualities, pour a little across, and continue with water (rain, rivers, sea, the body’s fluids and emotional tides), then fire and air likewise; for spirit improvise, for instance with a burst of laughter."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 96; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBSilentPrayerAndFearOfSayingFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Silent prayer and fear of saying it wrong"@en, "Stilles Gebet und Angst, Falsches zu sagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reluctance to speak freely, preferring silent prayer or pure imagination for fear of a wrong word, holds the practice back; here nothing can be said wrongly, since the deep mind supplies the words, and what counts is daring to speak."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of Invoking the elements in three speech stages; no deadline is set."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 96; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBThreeStagesOfElementalInvocationStages a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Three stages of elemental invocation"@en, "Drei Stufen der Elementanrufung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Describe the element; affirm unity with it; speak as it."@en ;
    skos:note "The series of the steps of pmp:ChaosMagicVmBInvokingElementsInThreeSpeechStages."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:ChaosMagicVmBDescribingWhatIsCalled ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:ChaosMagicVmBAffirmingUnityWithElement ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:ChaosMagicVmBSpeakingAsElement ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The source numbers the stages of the spoken invocation of an element: first description, then affirmation of unity, and as stage three speaking for the element; speaking as the element presupposes that it has been called up and felt as one with oneself." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 97; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBDescribingWhatIsCalled a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Describing what is called"@en, "Beschreiben des Gerufenen"@de ;
    skos:definition "First stage of the spoken elemental invocation: name and describe the element aloud in many images and qualities (for earth its fields, soil, rocks, colours, weight and the patience of stones), calling it to the rite."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the three-stage series of elemental invocation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 97; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBAffirmingUnityWithElement a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Affirming unity with the element"@en, "Bekräftigen der Einheit mit dem Element"@de ;
    skos:definition "Second stage: speak of the element as present and felt, in the landscape seen within and in one's own body, flesh and bone, until it and oneself are one."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the three-stage series of elemental invocation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 97; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBInvokingElementsInYieldsIdentityWithInvoked a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Invoking the elements in three speech stages yields Identity with the invoked force"@en, "Anrufung der Elemente in drei Redestufen ergibt Identität mit der angerufenen Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practice “Invoking the elements in three speech stages” is stated to produce “Identity with the invoked force”."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmBInvokingElementsInThreeSpeechStages ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmBIdentityWithInvokedForce ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 97; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBSpeakingAsElement a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Speaking as the element"@en, "Sprechen als das Element"@de ;
    skos:definition "Third stage: speak in the first person for the element, as its consciousness, saying that life grows from one's body and that one changes and yet remains."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the three-stage series of elemental invocation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 97-98; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBSpeakingFreelyAndBeingCarriedAwaySign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Speaking freely and being carried away"@en, "Frei sprechen und mitgerissen werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doing well means describing the element and speaking spontaneously and freely for some time; description and experience feed each other until imagination goes into overdrive and enthusiasm sweeps one along, the moment at which the magick lifts off."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of Invoking the elements in three speech stages; announced to the one practising and judged by the operator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 98; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBOrderOfElementsInCupPrayerScheme a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Order of elements in the cup prayer"@en, "Reihenfolge der Elemente im Kelchgebet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Earth, then water, then fire and air, then spirit."@en ;
    skos:note "An author-made scheme: Fries's own ordering for this book, not a series whose members take their sense from their place."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Jan Fries, in Visual Magick" ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> ;
