pmc:ChaosMagicVmBShakingAndTremblingAsSeidrTranceSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shaking and trembling as Seidr trance"@en, "Zittern und Beben als Seidr-Trance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shuddering, trembling, shaking, vibrating or jerking during prayer is no cause for alarm: it is seething (Seidr) trance, normal in older European nature religions before priesthoods insisted on dignity, and a favourable sign of flowing bio-energies and emotional and sexual power is released."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of Cup meditation (two-cup prayer); announced to the one practising and judged by the operator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 7 Imagination and Prayer, p. 102; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBReleasedPowerAsMediumGodsManifest a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Released power as the medium gods manifest in"@en, "Freigesetzte Kraft als Medium der Götter"@de ;
    skos:definition "This emotional and sexual energy is vital for magick and quite probably what gods and spirits need in order to manifest; more in the author’s books Helrunar and Seidways."@en ;
    skos:note "Strength in the source: quite probably."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
