#
# Chapter 8, Mandala Building
#

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBMandalaDefined a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mandala defined"@en, "Mandala bestimmt"@de ;
    skos:definition "A mandala is a map and a model of world and mind, and a potent visual device for invoking particular states of consciousness; like sigils and symbols it reaches the deep layers of the mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 105; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBTibetanSandMandalaRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Tibetan sand mandala ritual"@en, "Tibetisches Sandmandala-Ritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Observed in Munich, June 1989: call the house spirits to grant space and bless the ceremony; purify house and participants; burn incense, chant prayers, offer gifts to spirits of house and neighbourhood; invoke Avalokiteshvara; recite mantras in deep droning voices with bells; when the deity’s permission is sensed, stop chanting and begin measuring; draw circles, squares, lotuses and geometry on a wooden plinth; fill in colours by pouring coloured sand through metal-snouted tools, layer upon layer, over ten days, with the deity’s sign at the centre."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 105; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAvalokateshvaraNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Avalokiteshvara"@en, "Avalokiteshvara"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spirit of compassion and love, to whom the mandala is dedicated and whose palace it becomes; its sign stands at the centre."@en ;
    skos:note "Spelled so throughout the text layer; the usual form is Avalokiteshvara."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Avalokateshvara" ;
    pm:nameRole "spirit of love and compassion" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 105; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBSensedPermissionOfDeitySign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensed permission of the deity"@en, "Gespürte Erlaubnis der Gottheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The monks proceed from chanting to measuring once they sense that Avalokiteshvara consents."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of Tibetan sand mandala ritual; announced to the one practising and judged by the operator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 105; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBMandalaBuildingAsGestureForWorld a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mandala building as a gesture for the world"@en, "Mandalabau als Geste für die Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Building the sacred diagram in public belongs to the monks’ home ritual tradition and is meant as an offering to the world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 106; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBCureOfDiseaseWeaknessPovertyAnd a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cure of disease, weakness, poverty and ill-luck"@en, "Heilung von Krankheit, Schwäche, Armut und Unglück"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Callawaya rite is expected to cure the patient’s illness, weakness, poverty and misfortune; the healers hold that a mesa serves every purpose."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 106; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBCallawayaMesaHealingRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Callawaya Mesa healing ritual"@en, "Callawaya-Mesa-Heilritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bolivian healer: listen to and comfort the patient, consult an oracle; cover a crate with a whitish cloth; while praying aloud, lay out twelve small paper squares folded into containers (rectangle, groups or circle by village custom); put a nest-shaped cotton ball in each; adorn each with coca leaves, flowers, sweets, fruit, small lead figures and more as the patient can afford; grease an egg with llama fat for the Ankari; dedicate each nest to a power (house spirits, Catholic heaven, thunder god, ill-tempered spirits, sacred mountains); pray for hours; adorn and grease a llama foetus as offering; ask for healing and forgiveness and call all spirits known and unknown to forgive, partake and bless; charge a cup of strong alcohol and pour it on the Mesa and round the hut; pause half an hour or more chatting, smoking, drinking and laughing; later burn incense, purify the patient and ring a bell; finally burn the whole Mesa until nothing is recognisable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 106; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

