pmc:ChaosMagicVmBForgettingSacrificeIsDangerousCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Forgetting a sacrifice is dangerous"@en, "Ein vergessenes Opfer ist gefährlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the Bolivian belief system of spirits who demand offerings, omitting one can be dangerous, so the healer calls on all spirits, known or forgotten, to forgive and partake."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmBCallawayaMesaHealingRitual ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 107; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBMesaNeedsTimeAndForgettingToPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Mesa needs time and forgetting to work"@en, "Mesa braucht Zeit und Vergessen, um zu wirken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like a sigil, the completed Mesa has to be ignored for a while; it requires time and forgetfulness in order to act, hence the relaxed pause before the ritual resumes."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmBPauseOfForgettingAfterOfferingIs ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmBCureOfDiseaseWeaknessPovertyAnd ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without time and forgetting the Mesa does not take effect." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 107; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBPauseOfForgettingAfterOfferingIs a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Pause of forgetting after the offering is laid"@en, "Pause des Vergessens nach dem Auslegen der Gabe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once the Mesa (or a mandala offering) is complete and consecrated, leave it alone for at least half an hour: sit together eating, drinking, smoking, chatting, laughing, dancing or making music, paying it no attention, before the ritual resumes."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Written as the prior step of the Mesa's need for time and forgetting; the same pause is taken in the brass-plate mandala offering (p. 112)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 107; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBSeeingMesaBurnCanBeDangerousCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing the Mesa burn can be dangerous"@en, "Den Mesa-Brand zu sehen kann gefährlich sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many Callawayas believe it is dangerous for the patient, or anyone passing by, to watch the Mesa burning, so the healer often burns it alone."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmBCallawayaMesaHealingRitual ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 108; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBMandalaAsSacredAlignmentAndVisual a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mandala as sacred alignment and visual prayer"@en, "Mandala als heilige Ausrichtung und visuelles Gebet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Present in many traditions, the mandala is a sacred alignment, a perfected description of inner and outer universe, a prayer in visual form."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 108; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBLayingOutCircleAndAltarAs a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Laying out circle and altar as a mandala"@en, "Kreis und Altar als Mandala anlegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Arrange the circle and the altar tools deliberately rather than in a heap, so that the layout maps the self-aspects joining the working; make it balanced, simple and complex at once, and show the world in a healed, ideal state."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 108; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

