pmc:ChaosMagicVmBEverydayMandalasDecoratingCleaningArranging a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Everyday mandalas: decorating, cleaning, arranging"@en, "Alltagsmandalas: Dekorieren, Putzen, Ordnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Redecorating in times of crisis, calming housework, laying the breakfast table or ordering books are mandala building that invokes a kind of consciousness; some, however, keep a perfect home to avoid inner work, and Fries suspects inwardly balanced people are too busy enjoying life to perfect their homes. One may experiment with fresh alignments and enjoy the results."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 108; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBLughnasadHoopMandala a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Lughnasad hoop mandala"@en, "Lughnasad-Reifenmandala"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once a year around Lammas/Lughnasad in early August, go into fields and forests and bind a hoop of tough, long, flexible plants (mugwort, birch and willow twigs); add grains for next year’s nourishment and other plants, berries, cones and nuts, plus feathers, bristles, hair and small bones as nature’s gifts; from August to winter bind in further finds, consecrating each by talking about it and to it as it is cut and praying as it is bound, which links it to a memory and a purpose; keep the hoop at home; at the next Lughnasad bind a new one and burn the old."@en ;
    skos:note "Mugwort is chosen because its name is read as might, implying endurance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 109; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

