pmp:ChaosMagicVmBBrassPlateMandalaOffering a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Brass-plate mandala offering"@en, "Messingteller-Mandalaopfer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Go to the forest and pray to gods and spirits to send good material; gather through the day, speaking with each plant’s spirit about the rite and asking its blessing; sort at home; set a large brass plate on a wooden tripod (a big stone also serves; the metal plate matters); take one kind of growth after another and pray its symbolism (leaves: dying and rebirth; roots: earth, firmness, duration; fir twigs: life all year; nuts and seeds: hidden and coming life), placing each on the plate (about nine items fill an hour); consecrate the whole with the cup prayer, soaking mandala and room and drinking the rest; take a break for eating, drinking, dancing or music while it sinks in; resume prayer; finally drench it with pure alcohol and burn it, burying the remains the next day."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 110; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBCollectingMaterialInNature a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Collecting the material in nature"@en, "Sammeln des Materials in der Natur"@de ;
    skos:definition "Walk in the forest after praying to the gods and spirits to send good material, picking up twigs, leaves, cones, branches and the like, speaking with each plant's spirit about the rite and asking its blessing."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the seven-stage series of the mandala offering."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 110; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBGatheringMaterialAtHome a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Gathering the material at home"@en, "Zusammentragen des Materials zu Hause"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bring the finds home and sort them, ready to be taken up one kind after another."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the seven-stage series of the mandala offering."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 110; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBAligningItemsOnPlate a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Aligning the items on the plate"@en, "Ausrichten der Dinge auf der Platte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Place each item in turn on a brass plate (on a tripod or a large stone) until the plate carries a well-arranged heap of growth, the layout forming the mandala."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the seven-stage series of the mandala offering."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 110-112; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBDedicatingEachItemByPrayer a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dedicating each item by prayer"@en, "Weihen jedes Stücks durch Gebet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before an item is laid down, pray over it and invoke the power and meaning it holds for oneself (leaves for dying and rebirth, roots for earth and duration, fir for enduring life, nuts and seeds for life to come)."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en, "Stage node of the seven-stage series of the mandala offering."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 110; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBPersonalPlantMeaningMakesMagickWork a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal plant meaning makes the magick work"@en, "Persönliche Pflanzenbedeutung lässt die Magie wirken"@de ;
    skos:definition "The decisive symbolism is what each plant means to the practitioner, discovered through practice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
