pmc:ChaosMagicVmBBurningReleasesBoundIdeasIntoNew a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Burning releases bound ideas into new form"@en, "Verbrennen setzt gebundene Ideen in neue Form frei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Burning the ordered message releases the collected forces all at once; since no energy is lost, the ideas tied to the plants find new forms in which to manifest."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 112; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBDoctrineOfSignatures a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Doctrine of signatures"@en, "Signaturenlehre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Medieval healers held that every plant reveals its virtues by signatures; Paracelsus is cited to the effect that nature marks each growth to show its use and that bodily form arises from the inner arcane form."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries ascribes this to Paracelsus; the named source is reachable in its own right and is not read through him, so the node is entered as his ascription and not as a mediated reading."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 112; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmBSelectingPlantsForFourElementMandala a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Selecting plants for a four-element mandala"@en, "Pflanzenwahl für ein Vier-Elemente-Mandala"@de ;
    skos:definition "Earth: roots, dry old mushrooms, grains, berries and food plants (food for the body). Water: plants of wet places (willow, alder, poplar) and fresh sappy greens. Fire: blossoms (the plants’ sexual organs, vivid and warmer than the rest), tinder fungus, birch bark, fir cones as fire-starters, thistles and thorns for fighting power. Air: leaves and needles (the plants’ lungs), thin swaying grasses, berries as bird food, mistletoe and other parasites growing high. Colour can add symbolism."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 112; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBElementalPlantCorrespondencesScheme a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Elemental plant correspondences"@en, "Elementare Pflanzenentsprechungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author’s scheme assigning plant kinds to earth, water, fire and air by habitat, form and use."@en ;
    skos:note "An author-made scheme: Fries's own ordering for this book, not a series whose members take their sense from their place."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Jan Fries, in Visual Magick" ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 112; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmBSacredPlantsAsMeansToContact a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sacred plants as means to contact gods"@en, "Heilige Pflanzen als Mittel zur Götterkontaktaufnahme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many plants were held sacred to particular deities, so parts of them could serve to contact and invoke those gods; much northern lore was lost through persecution and renaming during the witch hunts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
