pmc:ChaosMagicVmBAlderLoreBranAndGreatGoddess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Alder lore: Bran and the great goddess"@en, "Erlenkunde: Bran und die Große Göttin"@de ;
    skos:definition "Robert Graves associates the alder with Bran’s cult; continental myth regards it as the great goddess’s tree from whom both sexes came; it bleeds red sap when cut, and its bark soaked with iron gives black dye."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries ascribes this to Robert Graves; the named source is reachable in its own right and is not read through him, so the node is entered as his ascription and not as a mediated reading."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 8 Mandala Building, p. 115; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

