#
# Visual Magick, unit 3 (chapters 9-11, pp. 123-179), integrated by reader C
#


#
# Chapter 9, Spirits of Nature
#

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSeeingElementalNatureSpirit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing an elemental nature spirit"@en, "Naturgeist schauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to call up and perceive an elemental or nature spirit (an in-between being) of a place."@en ;
    skos:note "The capacity is the one Master Recnartus asked Crowley for in the story Fries tells."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 123; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCPentagramTreeCallingRite a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Pentagram tree-calling rite (Crowley via Gregorius)"@en, "Pentagramm-Baumruf (Crowley nach Gregorius)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cut the (inverted) pentagram sigil at eye height with the magical dagger into a solitary or very old tree in a lonely spot, imagining the drawn sign as a summons radiating about seven km in every direction, charged by the will; cut it under the highest concentration of desire and imagination; best at twilight at full moon or in the first waxing phase; before leaving, erase the sign and thank the in-between beings."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Gregor A. Gregorius (Fraternitas Saturni), reporting instructions given by Aleister Crowley in 1925; the node holds his ascription, and the source he names is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, pp. 123-124; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCPentagramTreeCallingYieldsSeeingElementalNature a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Pentagram tree-calling rite yields seeing an elemental nature spirit"@en, "Pentagramm-Baumruf führt zu: Naturgeist schauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Fries's account the practice named pentagram tree-calling rite leads to the capacity named seeing an elemental nature spirit."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmCPentagramTreeCallingRite ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSeeingElementalNatureSpirit ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 123; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCTreeCallingRiteMayNotWorkFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tree-calling rite may not work at once; 49-evening term"@en, "Baumruf wirkt nicht sofort; Frist 49 Abende"@de ;
    skos:definition "The rite is said not to work necessarily on the first attempt; the novice should repeat it on at least 49 (7x7) evenings and, if nothing has happened by then, change to another tree."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: nothing after at least forty-nine evenings at the same tree. This sets a deadline: after seven times seven evenings without result the novice is to change the tree, so the failure is put on the tree and not on the rite or the operator; Fries passes it on as Fraternitas Saturni gossip."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCPentagramTreeCallingRite."@en, "Fries reports this from the gossip of the Fraternitas Saturni; the node holds his ascription, and the source he names is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 124; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCAgnosticismAboutWhatSpirit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Agnosticism about what a spirit is"@en, "Agnostik über das Wesen der Geister"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fries states he does not know what a spirit, a self or reality really is, and holds that practice does not require knowing; one interacts as with persons whose existence one never proves."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 124; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCNatureSpiritsExpressionsLifeForce a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Nature spirits as expressions of the life-force"@en, "Naturgeister als Ausdruck der Lebenskraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "A northern European model held nature spirits to express the life-force, residing in plants, trees, rocks, waters etc., giving growth and individuality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 124; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

