pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSpiritsReflectionsMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spirits as reflections of the mind (willow example)"@en, "Geister als Spiegelungen des Geistes"@de ;
    skos:definition "One interpretation: perceived reality is self-made, so tree spirits reflect those parts of our mind symbolised as tree consciousness; evoking a willow spirit contacts deep-mind parts that respond to willow associations (water, swaying, curves)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 126; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSelfKnowledgeThroughRockMountainSpirits a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-knowledge through rock and mountain spirits"@en, "Selbsterkenntnis durch Fels- und Berggeister"@de ;
    skos:definition "Evoking a rock spirit may disclose the parts of oneself able to rest, wait and be patient; evoking a mountain or forest spirit may connect one with a collective awareness, the awareness belonging to the whole biosphere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 126; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCPersonalSpiritsInternalNatureSpiritsIndependent a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal spirits internal, nature spirits independent"@en, "Persönliche Geister innen, Naturgeister unabhängig"@de ;
    skos:definition "A further model: guardian spirits, totem animals, allies and personal deities are mainly parts of the deep mind, while nature spirits exist independently; in both cases the perceived shape is made by our minds, so the two are hard to tell apart and need not be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 127; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCPragmaticTestSpiritContact a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pragmatic test of spirit contact"@en, "Pragmatischer Prüfstein des Geisterkontakts"@de ;
    skos:definition "What matters is not whether a spirit is inside or outside us but what the contact does: whether one learns, gains balance, healing or wholeness, enjoys it and is inspired."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 127; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSignsWorthwhileSpiritContactSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs of a worthwhile spirit contact"@en, "Zeichen eines fruchtbaren Geisterkontakts"@de ;
    skos:definition "A good contact shows in learning something new, finding balance, healing or becoming whole, enjoying it and being inspired."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: learning something new, finding balance or healing, becoming whole, enjoying the contact and being inspired. Judged by the operator alone; Fries offers it in place of deciding whether the spirit is part of oneself or of the local ecosystem."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 127; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCShamanicModelBiosphereLivingEntity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shamanic model: biosphere as one living entity"@en, "Schamanisches Modell: Biosphäre als ein Lebewesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ecosystem is viewed as a single living entity of interdependent life forms (paralleled in Maatian N'aton and the Gaia hypothesis); all life forms are aspects of one multi-personal all-self, so interaction between beings is the self communicating with itself, each form fulfilling a function for the whole."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 127; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCMindOrganisedLikeEcosystem a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mind organised like the ecosystem"@en, "Geist wie das Ökosystem geordnet"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the shamanic view the mind is organised like the ecosystem and the two mirror and affect each other (as in rain dances); the parts of the mind, harmonised by true will, appear as the spirits or deities of animals, plants, rocks, weather, ancestors and fabulous beasts; a beast spirit is an active part of the deep mind, a tree more passive, a rock almost beyond words."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 128; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCReadingMessagesFromNature a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reading messages from nature"@en, "Botschaften der Natur lesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When plants, beasts and stones carry meaning, natural events (a crow croaking on an oak, flying north) become specific messages from the deep mind or the shared sentience of the all-self."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 128; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCMandalaBuildingYearsPracticeMakeNature a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mandala building and years of practice make nature meaningful"@en, "Mandala-Ritus und Jahre der Praxis machen die Natur bedeutsam"@de ;
    skos:definition "The earlier mandala-building rite links plants to personal meanings; after years of practice the whole of nature carries meaning and can become a message."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered as a concept and not as a prerequisite: its prior step, the mandala-building rite, stands in an earlier chapter of the book (another unit of this harvest), so the link is named here and not drawn."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 129; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCTravellingThroughMindViaLandscape a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Travelling through the mind via the landscape"@en, "Durch den eigenen Geist reisen in der Landschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "In some trances shamans identify their surroundings so fully with their own minds that walking the land is travelling through the mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 129; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCMindLandscapeTranceCitiesCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Mind-landscape trance in cities"@en, "Geist-Landschaft-Trance in der Stadt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Such identification is wonderful in a forest but can be awful in a modern city; dissociate from places such as a supermarket."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmCTravellingThroughMindViaLandscape ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 129; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExerciseFourCreativeHallucination a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exercise four: creative hallucination"@en, "Übung vier: schöpferische Halluzination"@de ;
    skos:definition "Go into nature (countryside, forest, seaside, park or cemetery); relax and tune in, optionally inducing a pleasant trance; pick a striking stone or tree; ask what it means to you and what function it would have as part of your deep mind; then identify with it: contact it with all senses as intensely as possible, take much time, describe what you sense, slow down to its pace, ask how it rests, stands, sleeps or dreams, whether it perceives you, and imagine being it through years of weather."@en ;
    skos:note "Numbered as the fourth exercise of the book; the earlier exercises lie in other units."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 129; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCExerciseFourCreativeYieldsIdentifyingStoneTree a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Exercise four: creative hallucination yields identifying with a stone or tree"@en, "Übung vier: schöpferische Halluzination führt zu: Identifikation mit Stein oder Baum"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Fries's account the practice named exercise four: creative hallucination leads to the capacity named identifying with a stone or tree."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExerciseFourCreativeHallucination ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmCIdentifyingStoneTree ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 129; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCIdentifyingStoneTree a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Identifying with a stone or tree"@en, "Identifikation mit Stein oder Baum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Projecting human meaning into natural forms and feeling oneself as the rock or tree."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 131; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCSeeingTouching a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing as touching (tree posture)"@en, "Sehen als Tasten (Baumhaltung)"@de ;
    skos:definition "In trance in the woods, let the inner monologue fade, stare wide-eyed and empty-minded, and move the eyes over a tree so that seeing becomes feeling of bark, moss, pressure, twig angles, foliage; imagine your arms as its branches, read each gesture, take up the tree's posture with your body and name its meaning."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 131; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSeeingTouchingYieldsIdentifyingStoneTree a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing as touching yields identifying with a stone or tree"@en, "Sehen als Tasten führt zu: Identifikation mit Stein oder Baum"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Fries's account the practice named seeing as touching leads to the capacity named identifying with a stone or tree."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmCSeeingTouching ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmCIdentifyingStoneTree ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 131; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCProjectedMeaningHallucinationEffectReal a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Projected meaning is hallucination, its effect is real"@en, "Projizierte Bedeutung ist Halluzination, ihre Wirkung real"@de ;
    skos:definition "We cannot know what a tree feels; we attribute what such a posture would mean in us, exactly as we do with other people; what concerns us is the effect of the perceived message on our own mind, which is subjective yet real enough."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 131; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCReadingMeaningIntoPartnerFaceCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Reading meaning into a partner's face"@en, "Bedeutung in das Gesicht des Partners hineinlesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Assuming one knows what another person's tense face means is pure hallucination; leaping to conclusions and reacting hurt or upset is a habit to beware of."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmCProjectedMeaningHallucinationEffectReal ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 132; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCMoodTreeExercise a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Mood-tree exercise"@en, "Stimmungsbäume"@de ;
    skos:definition "Find trees that look sad or gloomy to you and spend time with them, observing the effect on your mood; then seek trees that look enchanted, powerful or magical and observe what it is like to be there."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 132; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCMoodTreeExerciseYieldsMoodChangeThrough a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Mood-tree exercise yields mood change through tree contact"@en, "Stimmungsbäume führt zu: Stimmungswandel durch Baumkontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Fries's account the practice named mood-tree exercise leads to the capacity named mood change through tree contact."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmCMoodTreeExercise ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmCMoodChangeThroughTreeContact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 132; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCMoodChangeThroughTreeContact a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mood change through tree contact"@en, "Stimmungswandel durch Baumkontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being among trees whose shapes the mind reads as sad or enchanted changes one's own mood; the enchantment is subjective but effective."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 132; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCSpittingWallCloudGazing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Spitting-wall / cloud gazing (Leonardo)"@en, "Spuckwand- und Wolkenschauen (Leonardo)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stare at length at a cracked, stained old wall, or, as Leonardo advised, at clouds in a relaxed posture, until scenes and figures appear; the relaxed posture helps trance or half-sleep set in."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this of others; the node holds his ascription."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 132; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSpittingWallCloudYieldsSeeingFiguresRandom a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Spitting-wall / cloud gazing yields seeing figures in random forms"@en, "Spuckwand- und Wolkenschauen führt zu: Gestalten in Zufallsformen sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Fries's account the practice named spitting-wall / cloud gazing leads to the capacity named seeing figures in random forms."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmCSpittingWallCloudGazing ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSeeingFiguresRandomForms ;
