pmc:ChaosMagicVmCReasonableNamingBlocksNewFormsFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reasonable naming blocks new forms"@en, "Vernünftiges Benennen blockiert neue Formen"@de ;
    skos:definition "As long as one keeps telling oneself it is just rock, cracks and moss, the mind sticks to that restrictive interpretation and no new forms are imagined."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the gazer keeps naming the surface in reasonable terms, rock, cracks and moss, and no new forms arise. No deadline; the cause is put on the operator's inner voice; observable only by introspection."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCGazingWithoutNaming."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 133; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCFiguresAppearAfterLongEnoughGazingSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Figures appear after long enough gazing"@en, "Gestalten erscheinen nach genügend langem Schauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one simply sees form long enough, figures and shapes will appear; may be hard at first, a developable skill."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: figures and shapes appearing in the surface after long enough gazing. Announced in advance and judged by the gazer alone; Fries grants it may be hard at first."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCGazingWithoutNaming."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
