pmc:ChaosMagicVmCOdinNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Odin (receiving the runes)"@en, "Odin (Empfang der Runen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Odin, the ancestral shaman god, who after fasting for days, exhausted on the tree, saw the random branches align into meaningful patterns and received the runes from them."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Odin" ;
    pm:nameRole "ancestral shaman god" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 134; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCExhaustionInnerSilenceFearStimulateImagination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Exhaustion, inner silence and fear stimulate imagination"@en, "Erschöpfung, innere Stille und Furcht wecken die Imagination"@de ;
    skos:definition "Exhaustion and inner silence are two ways to set imagination going; fear is a third."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 134; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCFearVisionIntensifier a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear as vision intensifier (Don Juan)"@en, "Furcht als Visionsverstärker (Don Juan)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deliberately frightening the apprentice (allies, night creatures, sorcerers) so that terror makes visions stronger and upsets an over-reasonable ego."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Carlos Castaneda, Don Juan books; the node holds his ascription, and the source he names is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 134; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCFearVisionIntensifierYieldsUnsettlingOverReasonable a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Fear as vision intensifier yields unsettling the over-reasonable ego"@en, "Furcht als Visionsverstärker führt zu: Das übervernünftige Ich erschüttern"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Fries's account the practice named fear as vision intensifier leads to the capacity named unsettling the over-reasonable ego."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmCFearVisionIntensifier ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmCUnsettlingOverReasonableEgo ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 134; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCUnsettlingOverReasonableEgo a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unsettling the over-reasonable ego"@en, "Das übervernünftige Ich erschüttern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Loosening an overly rational ego, thereby strengthening vision."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 134; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCReadingCrowleyNatureSpiritSigil a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reading Crowley's nature-spirit sigil"@en, "Deutung von Crowleys Naturgeistsigil"@de ;
    skos:definition "The inverted pentagram calls the spirits; its base bears an earth sign because nature spirits are sought; the moon sickles at the four elemental tips show the elemental spirits are to appear in the lunar realm of dream, reflection and imagination; a central beetle-like shape links it to Tarot Atu The Moon."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCPentagramTreeCallingRite."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 134; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSpiritVisionSubjectiveDaydream a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spirit vision is a subjective daydream"@en, "Geistervision als subjektiver Tagtraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "The nature spirit is seen with the eyes of imagination, like a vivid daydream; it takes a form fitting the seer's understanding, so two people may receive very different and equally right visions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 135; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCChasingAuthoritiesVisionsFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Chasing authorities' visions"@en, "Den Visionen der Autoritäten nachjagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many budding mages frustrate themselves by striving for exactly the visions that authorities report."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: striving for the very visions authorities report ends in frustration. No deadline; the cause is put on the operator's expectation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 135; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCVisionFormPlusMeaning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Vision = form plus meaning"@en, "Vision = Form plus Bedeutung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every vision has a perceived form and its meaning for the seer; the deep mind must choose forms that carry the right meaning for that person, so forms differ while meaning may be the same."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 135; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCVisionsIdenticalCastanedaIndicateSelfDeceptionFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Visions identical to Castaneda's indicate self-deception"@en, "Mit Castaneda identische Visionen deuten auf Selbsttäuschung"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one's visions match Castaneda's (or the author's) exactly, one is probably fooling oneself; Fries asks whether readers who tried to see Castaneda's holes in a person's aura or the shifting assemblage point took these for facts or for metaphors."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: visions that match Castaneda's, or the author's, exactly are taken as a sign of self-deception. No deadline; the test is the likeness itself, so the criterion is originality, judged against the reports of others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 135; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSeeingTreeSpirit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing a tree spirit"@en, "Einen Baumgeist schauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perceiving and communicating with the spirit of a tree, by image, sound or feeling, and receiving tree wisdom."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 135; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCHealthyLongKnownTreePrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "A healthy, long-known tree"@en, "Ein gesunder, lange vertrauter Baum"@de ;
    skos:definition "The tree-spirit evocation needs a tree, and choosing a strong, healthy one, ideally known and loved for years, is called a good start, since such a tree may house a spirit well disposed to the evoker."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmCChoosingTreeEvocation ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmCTreeSpiritEvocation ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 135; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCChoosingTreeEvocation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Choosing the tree for the evocation"@en, "Den Baum für die Evokation wählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "For the tree-spirit evocation choose a strong, healthy tree, best one known and loved for years, and avoid sick or stunted trees and those standing close to traffic or industry."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it as a node of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 135; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCDiseasedTreesTreesNearTrafficCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Diseased trees and trees near traffic"@en, "Kranke Bäume und Bäume an Verkehrswegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sick or stunted trees may produce difficult visions; trees near traffic or industry are unlikely to think well of people."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSeeingTreeSpirit ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 135; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSeasonalTimingTreeEvocation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seasonal timing of tree evocation"@en, "Jahreszeit der Baumevokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tree spirits are easier to contact in spring, summer and autumn when sap flows than in winter when awareness rests in the roots; evergreens and befriended trees can be evoked any time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 135; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCAcquaintanceTreePrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Acquaintance with the tree (49 evenings)"@en, "Vertrautheit mit dem Baum (49 Abende)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Become well acquainted with your tree first; Crowley's 49-fold repetition does exactly this."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmCPentagramTreeCallingRite ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmCTreeSpiritEvocation ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 137; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCPriorPracticeBookTechniques a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prior practice of the book's techniques"@en, "Vorherige Übung der Techniken des Buchs"@de ;
    skos:definition "Having practised the book's techniques makes success fairly likely; being able to invent one's own techniques puts one in a still better position."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered as a concept and not as a prerequisite: the prior step is the practice of the techniques of the whole book, which lie in earlier chapters; the order is one of presentation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 137; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCMagickAttitudeNotFixedTechniqueSet a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magick as attitude, not a fixed technique set"@en, "Magie als Haltung, kein festes Technikset"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fries says his technical advice becomes vague here; the book is not meant to found a new tradition of exercises; real magick is an open-minded attitude of interest and dedication by which each mage observes, learns, adapts and invents fresh means of transforming identity and reality from inside."@en ;
    skos:note "A statement on how fixed the methods are: deliberately not fixed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 137; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCEvocationActLoveUnion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evocation as act of love and union"@en, "Evokation als Akt der Liebe und Vereinigung"@de ;
    skos:definition "All evocation is an act of love: communicating with a hitherto unconscious aspect of the universe is an act of union; sympathy is the best link, the spirit understands mood if not words."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 137; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCTreeSpiritEvocation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Tree-spirit evocation"@en, "Baumgeist-Evokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Speak with the tree in genuine sympathy; embrace it, slow down, relax into gentle trance; call into it, declare your will to behold its spirit and ask kindly for a comprehensible shape; lean your head on it, look at the bark, close the eyes and imagine the bark as seen, reopening the eyes as needed until you see it with eyes closed; then imagine the bark transparent and look into the tree like a hollow tube, to roots and branches."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, pp. 137-138; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCTreeSpiritEvocationYieldsSeeingTreeSpirit a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tree-spirit evocation yields seeing a tree spirit"@en, "Baumgeist-Evokation führt zu: Einen Baumgeist schauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Fries's account the practice named tree-spirit evocation leads to the capacity named seeing a tree spirit."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmCTreeSpiritEvocation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSeeingTreeSpirit ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 137; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCEgoExpectationHidesResultFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ego expectation hides the result"@en, "Erwartung des Ich verdeckt das Ergebnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ego often expects the wrong event or looks the wrong way, so one may wait for something already happening in unrecognised form; whenever ego expects something specific, something vital is missed."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a specific expectation of the ego makes one miss or fail to recognise the spirit while it is already present. No deadline; the cause is put on the ego, and the same passage implies that an apparent failure may be a success not recognised."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCTreeSpiritEvocation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 138; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCFormsWhichTreeSpiritShowsItselfSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forms in which the tree spirit shows itself"@en, "Formen, in denen der Baumgeist erscheint"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some see the spirit at once; some see it humanoid; some perceive it by sound or touch before any image comes; some receive much tree wisdom without seeing a figure."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the tree spirit seen at once, seen in human form, heard or felt before an image comes, or given as tree wisdom without any figure. The range is so wide that hardly any outcome is excluded; judged by the operator alone."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCTreeSpiritEvocation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 138; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCTreeSpiritUnpredictableMayDeceiveCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The tree spirit is unpredictable and may deceive"@en, "Der Baumgeist ist unberechenbar und kann täuschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The spirit will not behave as expected: it may be moody, friendly or angry, appear in one form or a hundred, deceive or play with you, send strange insights or pretend to be absent."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSeeingTreeSpirit ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 138; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCImpatientEvaluationFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Impatient evaluation declares failure"@en, "Ungeduldige Auswertung erklärt das Scheitern"@de ;
    skos:definition "After a first partial result, impatient people analyse whether they did it right by asking ego if it matched expectations; then doubt, demands for instant results, feelings of incompetence and declaring the working a failure follow; the conscious mind cannot do the vision, the deep mind does, better when ego stops meddling."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: impatient evaluation of a first partial result against the ego's expectations, leading to doubt and to declaring the working failed. No deadline; Fries treats the declared failure as a product of the evaluation, not of the working."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCTreeSpiritEvocation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 138; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCHurryingPreventsIntegrationFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hurrying prevents integration"@en, "Eile verhindert die Integration"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invocation and evocation integrate long-latent parts of oneself, which can take months and years; excessive haste means one never gets there."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: haste; those who hurry too much are said never to make it. Not a deadline: months or years are given as the time the integration may take, not as a term after which the working counts as failed; the cause is put on the operator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 139; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCVariantsTreeSpiritContact a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Variants of tree-spirit contact"@en, "Varianten des Baumgeistkontakts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Alternatives: seeing through the transparent bark; a long detailed invocation, prayer or call; passive waiting; imagining walking into the tree and moving up and down inside the trunk until a being is met; transforming into a tree."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 139; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

