pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExerciseFiveShapeShiftingIntoTree a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exercise five: shape shifting into a tree"@en, "Übung fünf: Verwandlung in einen Baum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stand near the trees to be contacted, feet together, hands hanging; breathe deeply, relax, close eyes; slowly imagine becoming a tree: body as a pillar of wood layers with bark covering the skin, resting within; feel roots growing from the feet down through humus and stone to rock, drinking deep waters; feel sap rising through the stem; sway with the tree; feel branches growing from shoulders and head, twigs and foliage moving in wind under the sky; adapt the pattern to need."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries says the technique was already described in his Helrunar; the node holds the version given here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, pp. 139-141; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

