pmc:ChaosMagicVmCElementalContactWildBeforeIndoorsPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Elemental contact in the wild before indoors"@en, "Elementarkontakt draußen vor drinnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some can call fire spirits from a candle or earth spirits from a flowerpot, but whoever has first met the elementals outdoors, where they are strong and active, is said to know them well enough to reach them anywhere."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExposureElementElementalEvocation ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmCContactingElementalsAnySetting ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 143; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCContactingElementalsAnySetting a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Contacting elementals in any setting"@en, "Elementargeister an jedem Ort ansprechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Evoke elemental spirits away from their wild setting, fire spirits from a candle or earth spirits from a flowerpot; some are said to manage this, and anyone who has first met the elements outdoors is said to know them well enough to do it anywhere."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it as a node of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 143; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExposureElementElementalEvocation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exposure to the element for elemental evocation"@en, "Sich dem Element aussetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To evoke an elemental spirit, expose yourself to the element in natural form: e.g. sit by a stream hearing it, feeling its coolness, watching light, waves, bubbles and foam; in open country touch, smell and taste the soil."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 143; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCExposureElementElementalYieldsContactElementalSpirits a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Exposure to the element for elemental evocation yields contact with elemental spirits / recognising an element's essence"@en, "Sich dem Element aussetzen führt zu: Kontakt mit Elementargeistern / Wesen eines Elements erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Fries's account the practice named exposure to the element for elemental evocation leads to the capacity named contact with elemental spirits / recognising an element's essence."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExposureElementElementalEvocation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmCContactElementalSpiritsRecognisingElementEssence ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 143; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCCityEarthDiffersFromCountryEarth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "City earth differs from country earth"@en, "Stadterde unterscheidet sich von Landerde"@de ;
    skos:definition "Earth spirits of open country differ markedly from those of the city; abstract earth qualities (form, weight, solidity) are everywhere, but its life-giving virtues are, by practice, absent from concrete environments."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 143; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCContactElementalSpiritsRecognisingElementEssence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Contact with elemental spirits / recognising an element's essence"@en, "Kontakt mit Elementargeistern / Wesen eines Elements erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recognising the essence of an element in nature, as the spirit of a place, or within one's own nature, and meeting its spirits."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 143; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCContactArisesNaturallySign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Contact arises naturally"@en, "Kontakt stellt sich von selbst ein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Given a fitting mood and setting, contact may happen of its own accord."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: contact with the spirit of the element arising of itself in a fitting mood and setting. Judged by the operator alone."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExposureElementElementalEvocation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 143; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCTemperamentSpiritAffinityHarderElementWorth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Temperament and spirit affinity; the harder element is worth more"@en, "Temperament und Geistesverwandtschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Contact with some spirits is easier than with others according to temperament (a lusty person suits fire); the easy working is easy, but the uncongenial one is twice as valuable because it develops new self-aspects; each new spirit or god is a chance to develop a new self-aspect."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 144; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCFireSpiritEvocationCongruence a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Fire-spirit evocation by congruence"@en, "Feuergeist-Evokation durch Kongruenz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Light a large fire; dance round it, yelling and chanting until exhilarated and sweating; when very fiery, close the eyes, see the flames in imagination, summon the fire spirits; next imagine stepping right into the blaze, into a world of heat, light and intensity and meet the beings there."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 144; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCFireSpiritEvocationYieldsComingTermsFire a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Fire-spirit evocation by congruence yields coming to terms with one's fire aspects"@en, "Feuergeist-Evokation durch Kongruenz führt zu: Mit den eigenen Feueranteilen ins Reine kommen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Fries's account the practice named fire-spirit evocation by congruence leads to the capacity named coming to terms with one's fire aspects."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmCFireSpiritEvocationCongruence ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmCComingTermsFireAspects ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 144; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

