pmc:ChaosMagicVmCAirSpiritsAreFleetingCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Air spirits are fleeting"@en, "Luftgeister sind flüchtig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not expect air spirits to be as firm, vigorous or sharply defined as other spirits; they are fleeting and fast."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmCCongruentStatesEarthWaterAirSpirits ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 144; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCOneSidedFocusUpsetsBalanceCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "One-sided focus on one kind of spirit upsets balance"@en, "Einseitige Fixierung auf eine Geisterart"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each spirit is an expert on its own element and ignorant of the rest; focusing extensively on a single kind of spirit or god can seriously upset the balance; meet as many specialists as possible."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmCContactElementalSpiritsRecognisingElementEssence ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 144; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCReleaseExcessEnergyWhenLeavingElementPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Release excess energy when leaving an element"@en, "Überschussenergie beim Verlassen eines Elements abgeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one leaves the world of an element after an elemental working, the excess energy is to be released into its source, because healing needs the whole of one's living self; Fries leads from here into earthing."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmCFireSpiritEvocationCongruence, pmp:ChaosMagicVmCCongruentStatesEarthWaterAirSpirits ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEarthing ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 144; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEarthing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Earthing"@en, "Erden"@de ;
    skos:definition "If overloaded or upset after contact (e.g. with a tree spirit), touch the tree, thank its spirit and let the energy rush out back to its abode, imagining it vividly; or stretch the hands as high as possible, drop to the ground with a mighty howl, lie on the earth and, breath by breath, let the excess flow into the depths; take time and relax. At the close of rites, discharge the surplus into the ground."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 145; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCEarthingYieldsReleaseEnergyExcess a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Earthing yields release of energy excess; manifestation of the working"@en, "Erden führt zu: Abgabe von Energieüberschuss; Manifestation der Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Fries's account the practice named earthing leads to the capacity named release of energy excess; manifestation of the working."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEarthing ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmCReleaseEnergyExcessManifestationWorking ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 145; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCFeltOutflowDuringEarthingSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Felt outflow during earthing"@en, "Gespürtes Abfließen beim Erden"@de ;
    skos:definition "A clear bodily feeling of energy flowing out shows that it is working."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: a definite bodily sensation of outflow while earthing, said to tell the operator that all is going well."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 145; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCReleaseEnergyExcessManifestationWorking a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Release of energy excess; manifestation of the working"@en, "Abgabe von Energieüberschuss; Manifestation der Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Discharging overload after contact, and giving the working solidity so evoked forces take shape and manifest on earth; the released power carries the working's sentience, a child that begins to live once let go."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 145; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCAvoidingEarthingStagnationCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Avoiding earthing: stagnation"@en, "Unterlassenes Erden: Stagnation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Avoiding earthing leaves one bloated with unbalanced energies; hoarding power makes it stagnate and putrefy."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEarthing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 145; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCEarthingMostRitualsPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Earthing in most rituals"@en, "Erden in den meisten Ritualen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Earthing should form part of most rituals: it gives the working solidity so that the evoked forces can take shape and manifest; avoiding it leaves one bloated with unbalanced energies, and hoarded power stagnates and putrefies."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEarthing ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmCReleaseEnergyExcessManifestationWorking ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without earthing one becomes bloated with unbalanced energy; hoarded power stagnates and putrefies."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 9 Spirits of Nature, p. 145; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .


#
# Chapter 10, Waking the Beasts
#

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCModelsAreMapsNotReality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Models are maps, not reality"@en, "Modelle sind Landkarten, nicht Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gods, spirits, conscious and subconscious mind are metaphors describing how things can appear to us; the structures of consciousness are magical and psychological models that might or might not help, their efficiency depending on use."@en ;
    skos:note "A statement on how fixed the models are: maps whose use decides their worth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 147; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCNemaAllThatLivesIntelligent a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Nema: all that lives is intelligent"@en, "Nema: Alles Lebendige ist intelligent"@de ;
    skos:definition "Quoted proposal by Maggie/Nema: if everything lives and all life is intelligent, there may be mineral intelligence thinking slowly via crystal pressure changes, solar life thinking through plasma convection, and subatomic life."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Nema (Maggie Ingalls); the node holds his ascription, and the source he names is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 147; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCBothNeitherSpiritsAreOuterInner a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Both/neither: spirits are outer and inner"@en, "Sowohl-als-auch: Geister sind außen und innen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Either/or framing of inner projection versus independent being is too limited; contacting fire spirits contacts both the ancient sentience of fire and one's fiery parts (metabolism, power, lust, instinct); evocation reveals self-descriptions as artificial, self and all-self extending everywhere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 148; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCMindEcosystemSpiritsSymbolisedFunctions a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mind as ecosystem: spirits as symbolised functions"@en, "Geist als Ökosystem: Geister als symbolisierte Funktionen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Parts of the mind are described as spirits in natural or anthropomorphic shapes that represent their functions for easier comprehension by a conscious mind that thinks in common things."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 148; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCPartsMindFunctionalSpecialists a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Parts of the mind as functional specialists (hunger, sleep)"@en, "Teile des Geistes als Spezialisten (Hunger, Schlaf)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A part signals hunger and satiety, another signals need for sleep; each knows its conscious mind and uses signals that will motivate it; in shamanic symbolism the feeding part may be a crocodile, shark, wolf, bear or boar, the sleep part a hibernating or night beast; parts are unique per person and may function too weakly or too strongly (a hungry crocodile vs a squirrel spirit)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 149; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCKnowingExactlyWhichFoodNeeded a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing exactly which food is needed"@en, "Genau wissen, welche Nahrung man braucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "A well-developed feeding part can signal exactly which kinds of food the body needs; a skill to be developed."@en ;
    skos:note "Stated as a skill still to be developed; no method is given in this passage."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 149; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCHabitsDeepMindLearningMagickRelearning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Habits as deep-mind learning; magick as relearning"@en, "Gewohnheit als Lernen des Tiefengeists; Magie als Umlernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every habit was learned consciously once, then taken over by the deep mind; to adopt a better method one must unlearn the old, learn the new consciously, and if the deep mind accepts it, it becomes habitual; this is how magick transforms lives."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 150; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCUnlearningBeforeRelearningPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Unlearning before relearning"@en, "Verlernen vor Neulernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before a better way of doing something can work, the old habitual method has to be unlearned; only then is the new one learned consciously and, if the deep mind likes it, taken over as habit."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmCUnlearningHabitualMethod ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmCConsciouslyLearningNewMethod ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The new method cannot work while the old habit is in place."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 152; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCUnlearningHabitualMethod a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Unlearning the habitual method"@en, "Die gewohnte Methode verlernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unlearn the old way in which something is habitually done, as the first half of replacing it by a better one."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it as a node of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 152; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCConsciouslyLearningNewMethod a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Consciously learning the new method"@en, "Die neue Methode bewusst lernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Learn the better method consciously once the old one is unlearned, until the deep mind, if it likes it, takes it over as a habit; Fries calls this the way magick changes a life."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it as a node of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 152; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCLocusCoeruleusNovelty a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Locus coeruleus and novelty (Rossi)"@en, "Locus coeruleus und Neuheit (Rossi)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Quoting Rossi: noradrenergic neurons of the locus coeruleus respond to novel stimuli with brief heightened responsiveness in cortex and limbic reward centres, while dull repetition lowers activity and brings drowsiness; offered as a brain basis for a part that attends to the new."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from E. Rossi's book on the psychobiology of healing; the node holds his ascription, and the source he names is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 152; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCAncestorsEveryCellGeneticAggression a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ancestors in every cell; genetic aggression"@en, "Ahnen in jeder Zelle; genetische Aggression"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind holds genetically inherited aggressive programs from millions of years of animal ancestors; ancestor veneration (Voodoo, Taoism) is concrete: the ancestors, few of them human, can be met in every cell; much of this heritage is outdated, a source of political problems."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 153; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCAcceptingAggressivePartsBringsPeace a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting aggressive parts brings peace"@en, "Anerkennen der aggressiven Anteile bringt Frieden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recognising one's aggressive parts gives a good chance of a happy, peaceful life; aggression can give power to overcome obstacles and break restrictions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 154; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCUsingEmotionsSignals a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Using emotions as signals"@en, "Gefühle als Signale nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Understanding aggression and other strong emotions as messages from deep-mind parts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
