pmc:ChaosMagicVmCPartsUseWhateverWorks a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Parts use whatever works (need for attention and love)"@en, "Teile nutzen, was wirkt (Bedürfnis nach Zuwendung)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Parts of the mind use any method that produces the desired result; the shared need for attention and love is met by learned strategies (screaming, misbehaviour, charm); people make the best choice they know (Grinder and Bandler)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 155; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCPersonalityHabitualBehaviour a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personality as habitual behaviour"@en, "Persönlichkeit als gewohnheitsmäßiges Verhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "All behaviour is learned; habitual methods of meeting needs become automatic and create the illusion of a predictable, enduring personality; even problematic behaviour serves some purpose."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 157; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCChangingProblematicBehaviour a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Changing problematic behaviour (conjuring the part)"@en, "Problemverhalten ändern (den Teil beschwören)"@de ;
    skos:definition "First contact the mind-part that produces the behaviour by habit; then find alternative strategies that achieve the same need more efficiently; Bandler and Grinder (three named NLP books) recommended to improve this sorcerous practice of conjuring a spirit."@en ;
    skos:note "The order of its two steps, first getting in touch with the part that produces the behaviour, then finding alternative strategies, is the source's own; the extraction's separate prerequisite record for it is folded in here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 157; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

