pmc:ChaosMagicVmCDistrustDeepMindCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Distrust of the deep mind (Pandora's box)"@en, "Misstrauen gegen den Tiefengeist"@de ;
    skos:definition "People who treat the subconscious as a box of horrors do not trust it and it does not trust them."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSubconsciousBehavesBelieved ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 158; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSubconsciousBehavesBelieved a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The subconscious behaves as believed"@en, "Das Unbewusste verhält sich wie geglaubt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Nobody knows what the subconscious is, but it lives up to the metaphor used: as a junkyard of horrors (Freudian) it confirms that; called God it brings faith and miracles; called inner genius, Daemon or HGA it gives inspiration and help; Freud's deep mind produced neurosis, Jung's archetypes, Fries's a world changing under will."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 159; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCEachPersonMagicianCreatingBelievedWorld a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Each person a magician creating a believed world"@en, "Jeder ein Magier, der eine geglaubte Welt schafft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each deep mind produces whatever reality the conscious mind anticipates and reinforces through doubt, belief, pain and pleasure; we create a world, forget it is our making, and may remember."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 160; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCManyTitlesPhenomenonContactShapedBelief a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Many titles, one phenomenon; contact shaped by belief"@en, "Viele Namen, ein Phänomen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Behind divine, daemon, spirit helpers and deep mind lies one phenomenon too vast to comprehend; each name is a road of access, and contact will be as one believes; the rest is practice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 160; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCChoosingBeliefFrameTemperament a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Choosing a belief frame by temperament"@en, "Glaubensrahmen nach Temperament wählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beginners find trusting the gods easier than talking to a feared subconscious, and the gods' belief structure permits miracles; an atheist will be happier with a mind-parts or inner-genius model, which excludes miracles but has other advantages."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 160; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCNepaleseInitiationSealedSpiritHelpers a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Nepalese initiation with sealed spirit helpers"@en, "Nepalesische Initiation mit versiegelten Hilfsgeistern"@de ;
    skos:definition "A young shaman receives a group of spirit helpers (serpent, wild boar, silent dog and others) sealed by magic into bamboo tubes with food and liquids, and must learn to live with them through months of possessive trance and bestial urges until human and bestial aspects trust and transform each other."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this of others; the node holds his ascription."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 160; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCNepaleseInitiationSealedYieldsCooperationSpiritHelpers a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Nepalese initiation with sealed spirit helpers yields cooperation with spirit helpers as self-aspects"@en, "Nepalesische Initiation mit versiegelten Hilfsgeistern führt zu: Zusammenarbeit mit Hilfsgeistern als Selbstanteilen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Fries's account the practice named Nepalese initiation with sealed spirit helpers leads to the capacity named cooperation with spirit helpers as self-aspects."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmCNepaleseInitiationSealedSpiritHelpers ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmCCooperationSpiritHelpersSelfAspects ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 160; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCFirstMonthsSpiritHelpersAreWildCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "First months with spirit helpers are wild"@en, "Die ersten Monate mit Hilfsgeistern sind wild"@de ;
    skos:definition "The new spirits are untamed and overwhelming; in the first months they cause much trouble, outbursts, possessive trances, bestial urges and obsession releasing raw energy and emotion."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmCNepaleseInitiationSealedSpiritHelpers ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 160; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCCooperationSpiritHelpersSelfAspects a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cooperation with spirit helpers as self-aspects"@en, "Zusammenarbeit mit Hilfsgeistern als Selbstanteilen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The human and animal sides of the mind come to trust and change one another, giving a stable basis of magical cooperation; the spirits show themselves to be friends and self-aspects and the terror of obsession loses meaning."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 162; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCPossessionPersonality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Possession by personality (Martinie)"@en, "Besessenheit durch die Persönlichkeit (Martinie)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Quoted from Louis Martinie: the real issue is not possession by Loa, demons or angels but possession by personality; identification with personality is possession by limiting self-definitions; what people fear in ritual possession is the loosening of personality's hold, and ritual possession is a way to break out of an over-entrenched personality."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Louis Martinie, Cincinnati Journal of Magick VII, 1989; the node holds his ascription, and the source he names is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 162; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCBreakingFreeEntrenchedPersonality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Breaking free of an entrenched personality"@en, "Ausbruch aus einer verfestigten Persönlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ritual possession is said to be one way out of an over-entrenched personality."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Louis Martinie; the node holds his ascription, and the source he names is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 162; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

