pmc:ChaosMagicVmCHealingComesFromDeepMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing comes from the deep mind (Erickson)"@en, "Heilung kommt aus dem Tiefengeist (Erickson)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Psychologically, the shaman has developed subconscious parts for healing and sorcery; healing is assisted by the shaman but carried out by the system's gods and spirits, echoing Erickson's view that the therapist only creates a climate in which healing happens naturally."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Milton H. Erickson; the node holds his ascription, and the source he names is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 163; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCGuardianSpiritsMetaparts a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Guardian spirits as metaparts"@en, "Schutzgeister als Metateile"@de ;
    skos:definition "In shamanism guardian spirits function like metaparts, coordinating the parts that fulfil functions and produce behaviour."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
