pmp:ChaosMagicVmCAbraMelinOperation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Abra-Melin operation (summary)"@en, "Abramelin-Operation (Zusammenfassung)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Retire from the world to a secluded place; pray to the Holy Guardian Angel to appear and reveal itself, once daily in the first month, twice daily in the second, increasing until the whole day is devoted to the angel's communion; summed up as invoking often and inflaming oneself in prayer."@en ;
    skos:note "The month-by-month escalation (once daily, then twice, until the whole day is given to the angel) is a schedule and not a series of distinct stages, and the source is Fries's summary of another system; it is therefore not entered as a pm:Sequencing."@en, "Fries reports this from The Book of the Sacred Magic of Abra-Melin the Mage (Mathers); the node holds his ascription, and the source he names is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, pp. 163-164; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

