pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExerciseSixWakingTheBeasts a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exercise six: waking the beasts"@en, "Übung sechs: Die Tiere wecken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pattern in eight stages, to be changed at will: (0) spend hours imagining life with beast spirits, perhaps making a sigil asking the deep mind to reveal them, recalling childhood beasts, asking in trance for help invoking spirit guardians, praying and offering libations to the ancestors; (1) preparation: open your reality tunnel through confusion, exhaustion or ecstasy, choose a good day, take a long country walk to a private place exposed to the elements; (2) choose a place that feels good, arrive slightly tired and hungry, optionally lay out incense and food, draw a crossroads or gateway sign in flour or seeds, meditate briefly, greet the spirits of the place; (3) make music (bell, gong, tambourine, drum, rattles) and call with emotion and passion, not poetic words; (4) amplify: chant loudly, dance, scream, stomp, drum into exhaustion until body shakes, sweat runs and the mind spins, then close the eyes; (5) keep chanting as beasts appear; (6) integrate the beast by letting it into the body and enacting it; (7) make a pact; (8) afterwards give it plenty of fun."@en ;
    skos:note "The unnumbered preliminary (hours spent imagining life with beast spirits, a sigil, childhood beasts, trance, libations to the ancestors) precedes the eight numbered stages, which are entered as members of pmc:ChaosMagicVmCWakingTheBeastsSeries."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, pp. 167-172; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCExerciseSixWakingYieldsLivingWorkingBeast a pm:Yielding ;
