pmc:ChaosMagicVmCPassionOverTechnique a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Passion over technique"@en, "Leidenschaft vor Technik"@de ;
    skos:definition "The passion generated matters, not the technique; call wildly, emotionally and with devotion and trust the deep mind to transform."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExerciseSixWakingTheBeasts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 167; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCEarlyVisionDreamAnimalSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Early vision or dream of an animal"@en, "Frühe Vision oder Traum eines Tiers"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many get a first contact at the preliminary stage: a brief vivid vision or dream encounter with an animal, a greeting from the other side."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: a brief vivid vision or dream encounter with an animal at the preliminary stage of Exercise six; the next sentence denies that this is yet the contact."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExerciseSixWakingTheBeasts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 167; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCGreetingNotYetContactFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A greeting is not yet a contact"@en, "Ein Gruß ist noch kein Kontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first greeting does not mean success; a real, solid contact needs more commitment and work."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: taking the first greeting, a brief vision or dream of an animal, for the finished contact. No deadline; the remedy named is more commitment and work."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExerciseSixWakingTheBeasts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 167; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCWakingBeastsStageOnePreparation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exercise six, stage 1: preparation"@en, "Übung sechs, Stufe 1: Vorbereitung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Open the reality tunnel, that is one's identity, so that something new can come in, for instance by confusion, exhaustion or ecstasy; pick a good day, go far into the countryside on foot and look for a spot with some privacy that lies open to wind and weather. A wild setting is said to help greatly without being required; a skilled practitioner can produce the exhaustion indoors by dance and sex."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it as a node of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, pp. 167-168; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCWildSettingHelpsButNotEssential a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wild setting helps but is not essential"@en, "Wilde Umgebung hilft, ist aber nicht nötig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beast spirits thrive on nature contact and physical activity; an uncivilised setting makes calling easier, but skilled workers can produce exhaustion indoors by dancing and sex; a public park worked for the author's group."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 168; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCWakingBeastsStageTwoPlace a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exercise six, stage 2: choosing and preparing the place"@en, "Übung sechs, Stufe 2: den Ort wählen und bereiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pick a spot that feels right, which need not be real wilderness; come to it a little tired and somewhat hungry, states the beasts are said to understand; if wished, lay out incense and food of all kinds and mark a crossroads or gate sign on the ground with flour or seeds; a short meditation may gather the mind; before and after the working speak kindly to the place's spirits with a small prayer and an offering."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it as a node of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, pp. 168-169; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCResultsPublicParkOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Results in a public park"@en, "Ergebnisse in einem öffentlichen Park"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fries reports his group once performed the working in a city park and, after learning to ignore onlookers, got good results."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report: Fries's group performed the working once in a city park and, once they managed to ignore the onlookers, got good results; the results are not described."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 168; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCPowerSiteProstitutionCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Power-site prostitution"@en, "Kraftplatz-Prostitution"@de ;
    skos:definition "Esoteric tourists who use places of power without respect for their sentience and leave without thanks practise what Fries calls power-site prostitution; a power place is not a battery for all; where there is power there is sentience."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmCGreetingSpiritsPlace ;
