pmc:ChaosMagicVmCFriendlyRelationSpiritsPlace a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Friendly relation with spirits of a place"@en, "Freundschaft mit den Ortsgeistern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Signalling to the nature spirits that one comes as a friend."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 169; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCWakingBeastsStageThreeCall a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exercise six, stage 3: sending the call"@en, "Übung sechs, Stufe 3: den Ruf aussenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take up an instrument (bell, gong, tambourine, drum or a pair of rattles) and, while playing, send out the call; it has to match the animal sentience of the beasts, so it is made with emotion, passion and hunger in plain, crude, repeated words, not in poetic or intellectual phrasing."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it as a node of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 169; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCIntellectualCallingNotNoticedFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intellectual calling is not noticed"@en, "Intellektuelles Rufen wird nicht bemerkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Prayer to the beasts must be congruent with their animal sentience or they will not notice the call; poetic language and subtle definitions fail; they react to emotion, passion and hunger."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a call in poetic, subtle or intellectual words, which the beasts are said not to notice. No deadline; the cause is put on the manner of calling."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExerciseSixWakingTheBeasts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 169; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCTigerAfterAngerOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evocation that failed until anger (tiger)"@en, "Evokation, die bis zum Zorn scheiterte (Tiger)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fries recalls a caller who spoke only from the mind in fine words: nothing happened despite increased effort and commands; when he became truly angry at himself, a tiger appeared."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report: a caller who spoke only from the mind got nothing despite more effort and commands, until real anger at himself brought a tiger. It also carries a condition of failure, calling without felt emotion; no deadline."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExerciseSixWakingTheBeasts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 169; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCFeltSpeechBringsBeastsSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Felt speech brings the beasts"@en, "Gefühlte Rede ruft die Tiere"@de ;
    skos:definition "Words may be simple, crude and repetitive; if one feels what one says, with passion and hunger for union, the beasts will hear the call and arrive."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: felt speech, however simple and crude, is said to make the beasts hear and come."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 169; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCWakingBeastsStageFourAmplify a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exercise six, stage 4: amplifying the call"@en, "Übung sechs, Stufe 4: den Ruf verstärken"@de ;
    skos:definition "When the beasts are slow to come, strengthen the call: chant loud and with passion, play, dance, scream, stamp and drum without letting up, imagining the call spreading out beyond the known universe; go on into exhaustion until the body shakes, sweat pours and the mind starts to spin and a loud shamanic trance takes hold, then let the eyes close."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it as a node of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, pp. 169-170; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSignsAmplifiedCallSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs of the amplified call"@en, "Zeichen des verstärkten Rufs"@de ;
    skos:definition "Continue until you forget feeling strange, the body shakes, sweat runs and the mind spins; the released energy attracts the beasts and a loud shaman's trance sets in."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: forgetting the strangeness, the body shaking, sweat running and the mind spinning, then a loud shaman's trance; announced as the effect of the amplified call."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 170; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCWakingBeastsStageFiveKeepChanting a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exercise six, stage 5: chanting on while the beasts appear"@en, "Übung sechs, Stufe 5: weitersingen, während die Tiere erscheinen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Go on chanting as beasts begin to show in the imagination, some as quick glimpses and some more solid, and tell the wishful images from the real power beast, which is stronger than the conscious mind and has to be come to terms with, not controlled."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it as a node of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 170; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCWishfulThinkingBeastsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Wishful-thinking beasts"@en, "Wunschdenken-Tiere"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some beasts seen will be wishful thinking."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmCWakingBeastsStageFiveKeepChanting ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 170; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCTestsUnrealBeastFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tests for an unreal beast"@en, "Prüfzeichen für ein unechtes Tier"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wishful images are incomplete in expressive trance and do not touch strong emotion; if one watches the beast detachedly or ego thinks greedy thoughts of ownership and pride, it is not real enough."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the beast seen is incomplete, touches no strong emotion, is watched in a detached way or stirs greed and pride; then it is not real enough. No deadline; judged by the operator alone."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExerciseSixWakingTheBeasts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 170; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCRealPowerBeastFrightensEgoSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A real power beast frightens ego"@en, "Ein echtes Krafttier erschreckt das Ich"@de ;
    skos:definition "A real power beast makes ego squeak, appearing stronger than the conscious mind and threatening to take control; it cannot be controlled, only come to terms with."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: a real power beast makes the ego squeak, seeming stronger than the conscious mind and threatening to take control. Judged by the operator alone."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 170; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCIntegrationAfterConfrontationPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Integration after confrontation"@en, "Integration nach der Konfrontation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Confronting the power beast is not enough: it has to be integrated, most simply by letting it into the body and dancing and enacting it; only so does living with the beast begin."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEnactingBeastForm ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmCLivingWorkingBeastSpirits ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 170; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCRefusedBatOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Refused bat: vomiting and lost contact"@en, "Abgewehrte Fledermaus: Erbrechen und Kontaktverlust"@de ;
    skos:definition "A woman got a quick response (a bat through incense smoke) but found letting it in horrible and kept it out; she became violently sick, vomited, and never heard of the bat again."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report: a woman Fries knew refused to let the bat that came for her into her body, fell violently sick and has not heard of it since. It also carries a condition of failure, resisting integration; no deadline."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCExerciseSixWakingTheBeasts."@en, "Fries reports this of others; the node holds his ascription."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 170; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCCulturalConditioningAgainstPossessionCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Cultural conditioning against possession"@en, "Kulturelle Prägung gegen Besessenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Western conditioning to keep control whatever the price is a distinct disadvantage; in Voodoo possession is approved if by the right spirit; beasts behave beastly, some will upset you considerably."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEnactingBeastForm ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 171; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCDismembermentReconstructionPersonality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dismemberment as reconstruction of personality"@en, "Zerstückelung als Neubildung der Persönlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "In some shamanic traditions beast spirits first devour the shaman, later vomit the bones and remains and reassemble them until he lives again; Fries reads this as rebuilding a better-suited personality, one form of rebirth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 171; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEnactingBeastForm a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Enacting the beast form (association technique)"@en, "Verkörperung der Tiergestalt (Assoziationstechnik)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Either imagine the beast entering the body and lurking inside, then let it move, run, jump, scream and dance; or build a vivid picture of yourself transforming into the beast (process or superimposed images), make it attractive (large, vivid, clear, colourful, close), bring it close and step into it; then build an image of yourself even more possessed and associate again; repeat until satisfied."@en ;
    skos:note "Stage 6 (integration) of Exercise six."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 171; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCEnactingBeastFormYieldsLivingWorkingBeast a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Enacting the beast form yields living and working with beast spirits"@en, "Verkörperung der Tiergestalt führt zu: Mit Tiergeistern leben und arbeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Fries's account the practice named enacting the beast form leads to the capacity named living and working with beast spirits."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEnactingBeastForm ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmCLivingWorkingBeastSpirits ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 171; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCBeingMovedBeastDrasticCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Being moved by the beast is drastic"@en, "Vom Tier bewegt werden ist drastisch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sooner or later the beast moves you, which can be drastic; ego will dislike losing control and the body may be tossed about; go with it; human awareness may stay awake if it does not interfere: watch, do not meddle."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEnactingBeastForm ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 171; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCPactBeast a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Pact with the beast"@en, "Pakt mit dem Tier"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ask the beast if it consents to living and working with you and to collaborate in the great work, helping with the changes ahead."@en ;
    skos:note "Stage 7 of Exercise six."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 172; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCPactEssentialPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The pact is essential"@en, "Der Pakt ist unerlässlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "The pact is called an essential step, after which the beast helps discover and do true will."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicVmCPactBeast ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmCLivingWorkingBeastSpirits ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
