pmp:ChaosMagicVmCAftercareGivingBeastFun a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Aftercare: giving the beast fun"@en, "Nachsorge: Dem Tier Freude gönnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the following weeks let the beast have plenty of fun; transform and dance often; ask what it likes, learn its moods, desires, problem-solving style and above all its function for the whole being; do something good for the body."@en ;
    skos:note "Stage 8 (the time afterwards) of Exercise six."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 172; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCWakingTheBeastsSeries a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "The eight stages of Exercise six, waking the beasts"@en, "Die acht Stufen von Übung sechs, die Tiere wecken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Preparation, choosing the place, sending the call, amplifying it, chanting on while the beasts appear, integration, the pact and the weeks afterwards: the numbered stages in which Fries lays out the calling of beast spirits."@en ;
    skos:note "Numbered by the source itself, 1 to 8. Fries says the pattern may be changed at will, since what counts is the passion and not the technique. No consequence of skipping a stage is named except for integration, where the case of the refused bat (pmc:ChaosMagicVmCRefusedBatOutcome) is told; the source calls the pact an essential step without naming what follows if it is left out, so it stands as pm:prescribedOrder (pmc:ChaosMagicVmCPactEssentialPrerequisite)."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:ChaosMagicVmCWakingBeastsStageOnePreparation ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:ChaosMagicVmCWakingBeastsStageTwoPlace ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:ChaosMagicVmCWakingBeastsStageThreeCall ;
    rdf:_4 pmp:ChaosMagicVmCWakingBeastsStageFourAmplify ;
    rdf:_5 pmp:ChaosMagicVmCWakingBeastsStageFiveKeepChanting ;
    rdf:_6 pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEnactingBeastForm ;
    rdf:_7 pmp:ChaosMagicVmCPactBeast ;
    rdf:_8 pmp:ChaosMagicVmCAftercareGivingBeastFun ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Each stage rests on the one before it: the identity is opened first so that something new can come in, the place and the bodily state are prepared, the call is sent and then driven into exhaustion and trance, the beasts show themselves only while the chanting goes on, the one that comes is let into the body, the pact is made last, and the weeks after feed the contact that the pact has sealed." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, pp. 167-172; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCFrequentDancingStrengthensContactSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Frequent dancing strengthens the contact"@en, "Häufiges Tanzen stärkt den Kontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Frequent transformation and dancing strengthen the bond and make trance easier and more elegant; with less resistance cooperation becomes easier; drastic exhaustion is no longer needed once friends."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: frequent transformation and dancing strengthen the contact and let the trance come more easily and gracefully. Judged by the operator alone."@en, "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCAftercareGivingBeastFun."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 10 Waking the Beasts, p. 172; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCOneBeastNotEnoughCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "One beast is not enough"@en, "Ein Tier ist nicht genug"@de ;
    skos:definition "Limiting oneself to a single beast for safety is advised against; choice is needed; most practitioners work with several (Brazilian sorcerers chant a score into their belly)."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmCLivingWorkingBeastSpirits ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
