#
# Chapter 11, Coming to Earth
#

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCAgainstSingleTradition a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against a single tradition (Maatian multiplicity)"@en, "Gegen eine einzige Tradition (maatische Vielfalt)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The book succeeds if it gives readers the courage to build original new methods; the Maatian current works to avoid a single tradition, requiring maximally different points of view rather than one system, dogma or path of attainment."@en ;
    skos:note "A statement on how fixed the methods are: meant to be varied and reinvented."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 11 Coming to Earth, p. 175; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCImitationYieldsOnlyTechniqueCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Imitation yields only technique"@en, "Nachahmung bringt nur Technik"@de ;
    skos:definition "Simply imitating the book does no good; one acquires a few technical skills and it ends there."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmCAgainstSingleTradition ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 11 Coming to Earth, p. 176; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCReviewQuestionsWhatBookGaveSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Review questions on what the book gave"@en, "Prüffragen, was das Buch gebracht hat"@de ;
    skos:definition "Improved senses, imagination and skill with sigils, trance and prayer; more knowledge of the world one created and a better one; more discovered hidden self-aspects."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: Fries's own questions to the reader on what the book gave, better senses, imagination and skill with sigils, trance and prayer, a better self-made world, more hidden self-aspects found. Judged by the reader alone and after the fact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 11 Coming to Earth, p. 176; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCEarthingIntelligenceWellEnergy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Earthing intelligence as well as energy"@en, "Auch Intelligenz erden, nicht nur Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like falling to the ground to discharge energy, other gestures earth vision, information and intelligence; one cannot stay atop the mountain of initiation (Zen thirty-foot pole, Kether, nine nights on the tree), so one returns bearing the fire to give."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEarthing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 11 Coming to Earth, p. 176; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCMountainInitiationMetaphorMisleads a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mountain of initiation metaphor misleads"@en, "Bild vom Einweihungsberg führt irre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fries disputes the widespread metaphor among mages and witches of climbing a single-peaked mountain of initiation, saying it misleads."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered as a concept and not as a pm:Disputing: the other side is the unnamed users of the metaphor, and only Fries's side is read."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 11 Coming to Earth, p. 176; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCMagicalConstipationCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Magical constipation"@en, "Magische Verstopfung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mages who keep accumulating power, visions, secrets, titles, grades and initiations without giving out forget their obligation to the world and become clogged, bloated and poisoned."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicVmCEarthingIntelligenceWellEnergy ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 11 Coming to Earth, p. 177; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCCurrentMotionNotProperty a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A current is motion, not property"@en, "Ein Strom ist Bewegung, kein Besitz"@de ;
    skos:definition "A current cannot be owned or rationed to the faithful; to radiate it is to become empty or absent enough for it to manifest through one's whole personality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 11 Coming to Earth, p. 177; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEarthingIntelligenceThroughArt a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Earthing intelligence through art"@en, "Intelligenz durch Kunst erden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Communicate vision and realisation through art in any medium (painting, writing, sculpture, cooking, music, dance, theatre, festivity, film, programming); paint visions, let inner voices speak outwardly, express inner feeling in movement, posture, gesture, touch and love."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 11 Coming to Earth, pp. 177-179; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCEarthingIntelligenceThroughYieldsSharingMagickCommunication a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Earthing intelligence through art yields sharing magick by communication"@en, "Intelligenz durch Kunst erden führt zu: Magie durch Mitteilung teilen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Fries's account the practice named earthing intelligence through art leads to the capacity named sharing magick by communication."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicVmCEarthingIntelligenceThroughArt ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSharingMagickCommunication ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
