pmc:ChaosMagicVmCArtBypassesEgoCensors a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Art bypasses the ego's censors (Nema)"@en, "Kunst umgeht die Zensur des Ich (Nema)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Quoted from Nema: art moves and changes an audience by slipping past the verbal censorship of an unbalanced ego; a good artist knows which responses to evoke and how; art shows rather than tells; all great artists function as priests."@en ;
    skos:note "Fries reports this from Nema, The Priesthood; the node holds his ascription, and the source he names is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 11 Coming to Earth, p. 177; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCGuardianAngelBeforeArtCommunion a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Contact with the Guardian Angel before communion through art"@en, "Kontakt zum Schutzengel vor der Kommunion durch Kunst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Communion through art is said to begin once the mage has some contact with the Guardian Angel in Tiphareth and begins to see what the true will is, which then expresses itself through art."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmCKnowledgeConversationHolyGuardianAngel ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSharingMagickCommunication ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 11 Coming to Earth, p. 178; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCArtificialEgoPersonalityFirstWorkArt a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Artificial ego: personality as first work of art"@en, "Künstliches Ich: Persönlichkeit als erstes Kunstwerk"@de ;
    skos:definition "The newborn adept's first work of art is his or her own personality, created to do the true will (an artificial ego designed for specific tasks); living one's true will makes one a living talisman for humanity (Nema); identities are masks created, worn and discarded, there being no final mask."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 11 Coming to Earth, p. 178; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCFreelyChosenIdentityReality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freely chosen identity and reality"@en, "Frei gewählte Identität und Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "By continuously creating identity, the mage shows that identity and reality are open to choice and made as love and will require; living in accord with one's visions lets them transform the outer world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
    dcterms:source "Fries, Visual Magick: A Practical Guide to Trance, Sigils and Visualization Techniques (Oxford: Mandrake of Oxford, copyright 1992; a later printing with ISBN 978-1-869928-57-5), chapter 11 Coming to Earth, p. 178; read in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item JanFries-visual-magick-1992" .

pmc:ChaosMagicVmCSharingMagickCommunication a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sharing magick by communication"@en, "Magie durch Mitteilung teilen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Communicating experience so it moves others; communication as sacrament, union of intelligence with intelligence, whose offspring is a fresh state of consciousness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VisualMagick ;
